window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b014-c893741e26c64fdc.json"]={sha256:"c893741e26c64fdcfdbaeecef62a93d60a488680ec575f2beac77a0413b23e29",value:{"id":"b014","title":"聯邦大橋（加拿大）","titleEn":"Confederation Bridge","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"聯邦大橋連接愛德華王子島與新布倫瑞克省，全長約 12.9 公里，是跨越冬季結冰海域最長的橋梁，主橋段以約 250 公尺的跨徑排列，設計壽命 100 年。本課從浮冰荷載與冰盾錐體出發，拆解主梁懸臂與掛梁組成的預製體系、高性能混凝土與墩身接合，再看陸上預製場、浮吊 Svanen 與高峰期每週一跨的安裝節奏，最後談冰力監測、強風管制、除冰鹽與凍融，以及 2032 年特許營運結束時的交接。","summaryEn":"Confederation Bridge links Prince Edward Island and New Brunswick over about 12.9 km, the longest bridge over ice-covered water, with main spans of about 250 m and a 100-year design life. Starting from pack-ice loads and the ice-shield cones, the course unpacks the precast system of cantilevered main girders and drop-in spans, high-performance concrete and pier joints, then the land casting yard, the floating crane Svanen and a peak rate of one span a week, ending with ice-force monitoring, wind restrictions, de-icing salt and freeze–thaw, and the handover when the concession ends in 2032.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-arch-viaduct-sea","subcategoryTitle":"拱橋、高架橋與跨海通道","subcategoryTitleEn":"Arch bridges, viaducts and sea crossings","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-arch-viaduct-sea","learningTags":["structures","st-arch-viaduct-sea","viaduct"],"architectureFamily":"viaduct","architectureNodes":[["預製墩座與海床","Precast pier bases on the seabed"],["墩身與冰盾錐體","Pier shafts and ice-shield cones"],["主梁懸臂與預力","Main girder cantilevers and prestress"],["掛梁與伸縮裝置","Drop-in spans and expansion devices"],["橋面防水與鋪面","Deck waterproofing and surfacing"],["冰力、風速監測與檢查紀錄","Ice and wind monitoring and inspection records"]],"architectureEdges":[[3,2],[2,1],[1,0],[4,2],[4,3],[5,1],[5,4]],"diagram":{"type":"viaduct","labels":["預製墩座與海床","墩身與冰盾錐體","主梁懸臂與預力","掛梁與伸縮裝置","橋面防水與鋪面"],"labelsEn":["Precast pier bases on the seabed","Pier shafts and ice-shield cones","Main girder cantilevers and prestress","Drop-in spans and expansion devices","Deck waterproofing and surfacing"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"冰盾設計練習：某主墩水線寬 D = 14 m，設計冰厚 h = 0.6 m。垂直面壓碎力 F_c = σ_c·h·D = 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN；錐面彎曲破壞力 F_b = k·σ_f·h² = 10×0.7×0.6² ≈ 2.52 MN。冰力作用點到墩座接合面的力臂取 25 m，彎矩分別為 16.8×25 = 420 MN·m 與 2.52×25 = 63 MN·m。接合面面積 A = 40 m²、斷面模數 S = 60 m³，彎曲應力分別為 420/60 = 7.0 MPa 與 63/60 = 1.05 MPa。若上方主梁重 7,500 t（約 73.6 MN），平均壓應力 73.6/40 ≈ 1.84 MPa：錐面情況下 1.84 > 1.05，接合面不會張開；垂直面情況下需再增加約 (7.0 − 1.84)×40 ≈ 206 MN 的預力才能保持全斷面受壓。結論是冰盾錐體大幅減少了墩身與接合面所需的預力。數值為教學假設，不代表聯邦大橋的設計。","textEn":"Ice-shield exercise: a main pier is D = 14 m wide at the waterline with design ice thickness h = 0.6 m. Crushing on a vertical face gives F_c = σ_c·h·D = 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN; bending failure on a cone gives F_b = k·σ_f·h² = 10×0.7×0.6² ≈ 2.52 MN. With a 25 m lever arm to the base joint, the moments are 16.8×25 = 420 MN·m and 2.52×25 = 63 MN·m. For a joint area A = 40 m² and section modulus S = 60 m³, the bending stresses are 420/60 = 7.0 MPa and 63/60 = 1.05 MPa. A 7,500 t girder above (about 73.6 MN) gives an average compression of 73.6/40 ≈ 1.84 MPa: with the cone, 1.84 > 1.05 and the joint stays closed; with a vertical face about (7.0 − 1.84)×40 ≈ 206 MN of extra prestress would be needed to keep the section in compression. The cone therefore greatly reduces the prestress demand on shaft and joint. Values are teaching assumptions, not the Confederation Bridge design.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b014-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「海峽浮冰與冰盾錐體」與「250 公尺主跨的預製構件體系」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pack ice and the ice-shield cones\" and \"Precast system for the 250 m spans\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b014-v13-01","title":"海峽浮冰與冰盾錐體：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Pack ice and the ice-shield cones: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「冰盾錐體」如何影響聯邦大橋（加拿大）的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ice-shield cone” governs force, deformation or durability in “Confederation Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"諾森伯蘭海峽每年冬季被浮冰覆蓋，冰板隨潮流與風移動，撞到橋墩時會產生很大的水平力。若墩身在水線處是垂直面，冰板只能被壓碎，力量由冰的抗壓強度決定；聯邦大橋在每座墩的水線處設置錐形冰盾，讓冰板沿斜面爬升而以彎曲方式斷裂，冰的抗彎強度遠低於抗壓強度，因此傳到墩身的力大幅降低。錐體也讓碎冰順利從墩旁流走，避免冰塊在墩前堆積造成更大的推力或阻塞海流。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「冰盾錐體」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Northumberland Strait is covered in pack ice every winter, and ice sheets driven by tide and wind exert large horizontal forces on piers. With a vertical face at the waterline the ice can only crush, with force set by its compressive strength; Confederation Bridge has a conical ice shield at the waterline of each pier so that the sheet rides up the slope and fails in bending, and because ice is far weaker in bending than in compression, the force on the pier drops sharply. The cone also lets broken ice clear past the pier instead of piling up in front of it, where rubble would push harder and obstruct the flow. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Ice-shield cone” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：垂直面壓碎力 F_c ≈ σ_c·h·D：σ_c = 2.0 MPa、冰厚 h = 0.6 m、水線寬 D = 14 m，F_c ≈ 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Crushing on a vertical face F_c ≈ σ_c·h·D: with σ_c = 2.0 MPa, ice thickness h = 0.6 m and waterline width D = 14 m, F_c ≈ 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「冰比混凝土軟得多，所以浮冰對橋墩的力量可以忽略。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Ice is much softer than concrete, so pack-ice forces on piers are negligible.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「冰盾錐體」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Ice-shield cone”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-01-k1","title":"海峽浮冰與冰盾錐體","titleEn":"Pack ice and the ice-shield cones","text":"諾森伯蘭海峽每年冬季被浮冰覆蓋，冰板隨潮流與風移動，撞到橋墩時會產生很大的水平力。若墩身在水線處是垂直面，冰板只能被壓碎，力量由冰的抗壓強度決定；聯邦大橋在每座墩的水線處設置錐形冰盾，讓冰板沿斜面爬升而以彎曲方式斷裂，冰的抗彎強度遠低於抗壓強度，因此傳到墩身的力大幅降低。","textEn":"The Northumberland Strait is covered in pack ice every winter, and ice sheets driven by tide and wind exert large horizontal forces on piers. With a vertical face at the waterline the ice can only crush, with force set by its compressive strength; Confederation Bridge has a conical ice shield at the waterline of each pier so that the sheet rides up the slope and fails in bending, and because ice is far weaker in bending than in compression, the force on the pier drops sharply.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：冰比混凝土軟得多，所以浮冰對橋墩的力量可以忽略。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Ice is much softer than concrete, so pack-ice forces on piers are negligible. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「海峽浮冰與冰盾錐體」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pack ice and the ice-shield cones\" is correct?","options":["冰比混凝土軟得多，所以浮冰對橋墩的力量可以忽略。","諾森伯蘭海峽每年冬季被浮冰覆蓋，冰板隨潮流與風移動，撞到橋墩時會產生很大的水平力。","預製構件只要在陸上做好，放到墩上就完成了結構體系。"],"optionsEn":["Ice is much softer than concrete, so pack-ice forces on piers are negligible.","The Northumberland Strait is covered in pack ice every winter, and ice sheets driven by tide and wind exert large horizontal forces on piers.","Once precast pieces are made on land and set on the piers, the structural system is complete."],"answer":1,"explanation":"諾森伯蘭海峽每年冬季被浮冰覆蓋，冰板隨潮流與風移動，撞到橋墩時會產生很大的水平力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Northumberland Strait is covered in pack ice every winter, and ice sheets driven by tide and wind exert large horizontal forces on piers. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b014-v13-02","title":"海峽浮冰與冰盾錐體：定量估算","titleEn":"Pack ice and the ice-shield cones: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「冰盾錐體」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ice-shield cone” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：垂直面壓碎力 F_c ≈ σ_c·h·D：σ_c = 2.0 MPa、冰厚 h = 0.6 m、水線寬 D = 14 m，F_c ≈ 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN。錐面彎曲破壞力以簡化式 F_b ≈ k·σ_f·h²：k = 10、σ_f = 0.7 MPa，F_b ≈ 10×0.7×0.6² ≈ 2.52 MN，約為壓碎力的 1/6.7。所有參數為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Crushing on a vertical face F_c ≈ σ_c·h·D: with σ_c = 2.0 MPa, ice thickness h = 0.6 m and waterline width D = 14 m, F_c ≈ 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN. Bending failure on a cone, by a simplified F_b ≈ k·σ_f·h² with k = 10 and σ_f = 0.7 MPa, gives F_b ≈ 10×0.7×0.6² ≈ 2.52 MN, about 1/6.7 of the crushing force. All parameters are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：設計時以海冰觀測資料統計冰厚、冰速與冰強度，並以冰槽模型試驗或數值模擬比較錐體與垂直面的冰力；營運期在代表性墩位量測墩身傾斜、加速度或應變，配合冰況觀測反算實際冰力，與設計值比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At design stage derive ice thickness, speed and strength statistics from observations and compare cone and vertical-face ice forces in ice-tank model tests or simulations; in service measure tilt, acceleration or strain on representative piers and back-calculate actual ice forces from observed ice conditions for comparison with design.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"垂直面壓碎力 F_c ≈ σ_c·h·D：σ_c = 2.0 MPa、冰厚 h = 0.6 m、水線寬 D = 14 m，F_c ≈ 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN。錐面彎曲破壞力以簡化式 F_b ≈ k·σ_f·h²：k = 10、σ_f = 0.7 MPa，F_b ≈ 10×0.7×0.6² ≈ 2.52 MN，約為壓碎力的 1/6.7。所有參數為教學假設。","textEn":"Crushing on a vertical face F_c ≈ σ_c·h·D: with σ_c = 2.0 MPa, ice thickness h = 0.6 m and waterline width D = 14 m, F_c ≈ 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN. Bending failure on a cone, by a simplified F_b ≈ k·σ_f·h² with k = 10 and σ_f = 0.7 MPa, gives F_b ≈ 10×0.7×0.6² ≈ 2.52 MN, about 1/6.7 of the crushing force. All parameters are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「海峽浮冰與冰盾錐體」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pack ice and the ice-shield cones\", which statement holds?","options":["預製構件夠重，疊上去後不需要灌漿或預力就能穩定傳力。","預製構件尺寸精準，放上去後的高程就不會再改變。","垂直面壓碎力 F_c ≈ σ_c·h·D：σ_c = 2.0 MPa、冰厚 h = 0.6 m、水線寬 D = 14 m，F_c ≈ 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN。"],"optionsEn":["Precast pieces are heavy enough to transmit load reliably when stacked, without grout or prestress.","Precast pieces are accurate, so their levels stay fixed after placement.","Crushing on a vertical face F_c ≈ σ_c·h·D: with σ_c = 2.0 MPa, ice thickness h = 0.6 m and waterline width D = 14 m, F_c ≈ 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"垂直面壓碎力 F_c ≈ σ_c·h·D：σ_c = 2.0 MPa、冰厚 h = 0.6 m、水線寬 D = 14 m，F_c ≈ 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Crushing on a vertical face F_c ≈ σ_c·h·D: with σ_c = 2.0 MPa, ice thickness h = 0.6 m and waterline width D = 14 m, F_c ≈ 2.0×0.6×14 = 16.8 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b014-v13-03","title":"海峽浮冰與冰盾錐體：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pack ice and the ice-shield cones: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「冰盾錐體」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ice-shield cone” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"設計時以海冰觀測資料統計冰厚、冰速與冰強度，並以冰槽模型試驗或數值模擬比較錐體與垂直面的冰力；營運期在代表性墩位量測墩身傾斜、加速度或應變，配合冰況觀測反算實際冰力，與設計值比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At design stage derive ice thickness, speed and strength statistics from observations and compare cone and vertical-face ice forces in ice-tank model tests or simulations; in service measure tilt, acceleration or strain on representative piers and back-calculate actual ice forces from observed ice conditions for comparison with design. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：冰區橋梁的設計基準應明列冰厚、冰強度、冰速與水位組合，冰盾的有效高程範圍要涵蓋設計潮差與風暴潮；營運手冊規定冰季巡查項目，例如墩前冰堆積、錐面磨損與異常振動。","observationEn":"Site practice: The design basis for an ice-exposed bridge should list combinations of ice thickness, strength, speed and water level, and the cone's effective elevation range must cover design tides and storm surge; the operating manual sets ice-season patrol items such as rubble build-up, cone wear and unusual vibration.","failure":"注意干擾：若冰盾角度或位置與實際水位、潮差不配合，冰板在高潮或低潮時打到錐體以外的垂直墩身，力量回到壓碎模式；冰塊在墩前堆積成冰脊時，作用力與作用高度都超出單層冰板的假設，墩身承受額外彎矩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the cone angle or elevation does not match actual water levels and tides, ice strikes the vertical shaft above or below the cone at high or low water and the force returns to crushing; rubble ridges piling in front of a pier exceed the single-sheet assumption in both force and height, adding bending to the shaft. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"設計時以海冰觀測資料統計冰厚、冰速與冰強度，並以冰槽模型試驗或數值模擬比較錐體與垂直面的冰力；營運期在代表性墩位量測墩身傾斜、加速度或應變，配合冰況觀測反算實際冰力，與設計值比較。","textEn":"At design stage derive ice thickness, speed and strength statistics from observations and compare cone and vertical-face ice forces in ice-tank model tests or simulations; in service measure tilt, acceleration or strain on representative piers and back-calculate actual ice forces from observed ice conditions for comparison with design.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"冰區橋梁的設計基準應明列冰厚、冰強度、冰速與水位組合，冰盾的有效高程範圍要涵蓋設計潮差與風暴潮；營運手冊規定冰季巡查項目，例如墩前冰堆積、錐面磨損與異常振動。","textEn":"The design basis for an ice-exposed bridge should list combinations of ice thickness, strength, speed and water level, and the cone's effective elevation range must cover design tides and storm surge; the operating manual sets ice-season patrol items such as rubble build-up, cone wear and unusual vibration.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「海峽浮冰與冰盾錐體」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pack ice and the ice-shield cones\"?","options":["設計時以海冰觀測資料統計冰厚、冰速與冰強度，並以冰槽模型試驗或數值模擬比較錐體與垂直面的冰力。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要橋梁結構能承受颱風等級的風，車輛在橋上就一定安全。"],"optionsEn":["At design stage derive ice thickness, speed and strength statistics from observations and compare cone and vertical-face ice forces in ice-tank model tests or simulations.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If the structure can withstand storm winds, vehicles on it are automatically safe."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設計時以海冰觀測資料統計冰厚、冰速與冰強度，並以冰槽模型試驗或數值模擬比較錐體與垂直面的冰力；營運期在代表性墩位量測墩身傾斜、加速度或應變，配合冰況觀測反算實際冰力，與設計值比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"At design stage derive ice thickness, speed and strength statistics from observations and compare cone and vertical-face ice forces in ice-tank model tests or simulations; in service measure tilt, acceleration or strain on representative piers and back-calculate actual ice forces from observed ice conditions for comparison with design. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b014-v13-04","title":"海峽浮冰與冰盾錐體：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pack ice and the ice-shield cones: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「冰盾錐體」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ice-shield cone” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若冰盾角度或位置與實際水位、潮差不配合，冰板在高潮或低潮時打到錐體以外的垂直墩身，力量回到壓碎模式；冰塊在墩前堆積成冰脊時，作用力與作用高度都超出單層冰板的假設，墩身承受額外彎矩。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the cone angle or elevation does not match actual water levels and tides, ice strikes the vertical shaft above or below the cone at high or low water and the force returns to crushing; rubble ridges piling in front of a pier exceed the single-sheet assumption in both force and height, adding bending to the shaft. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：錐體也讓碎冰順利從墩旁流走，避免冰塊在墩前堆積造成更大的推力或阻塞海流。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The cone also lets broken ice clear past the pier instead of piling up in front of it, where rubble would push harder and obstruct the flow.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「冰比混凝土軟得多，所以浮冰對橋墩的力量可以忽略。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Ice is much softer than concrete, so pack-ice forces on piers are negligible.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若冰盾角度或位置與實際水位、潮差不配合，冰板在高潮或低潮時打到錐體以外的垂直墩身，力量回到壓碎模式；冰塊在墩前堆積成冰脊時，作用力與作用高度都超出單層冰板的假設，墩身承受額外彎矩。","textEn":"If the cone angle or elevation does not match actual water levels and tides, ice strikes the vertical shaft above or below the cone at high or low water and the force returns to crushing; rubble ridges piling in front of a pier exceed the single-sheet assumption in both force and height, adding bending to the shaft.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「海峽浮冰與冰盾錐體」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pack ice and the ice-shield cones\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若冰盾角度或位置與實際水位、潮差不配合，冰板在高潮或低潮時打到錐體以外的垂直墩身，力量回到壓碎模式。","預製構件只要在陸上做好，放到墩上就完成了結構體系。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","If the cone angle or elevation does not match actual water levels and tides, ice strikes the vertical shaft above or below the cone at high or low water and the force returns to crushing.","Once precast pieces are made on land and set on the piers, the structural system is complete."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若冰盾角度或位置與實際水位、潮差不配合，冰板在高潮或低潮時打到錐體以外的垂直墩身，力量回到壓碎模式；冰塊在墩前堆積成冰脊時，作用力與作用高度都超出單層冰板的假設，墩身承受額外彎矩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the cone angle or elevation does not match actual water levels and tides, ice strikes the vertical shaft above or below the cone at high or low water and the force returns to crushing; rubble ridges piling in front of a pier exceed the single-sheet assumption in both force and height, adding bending to the shaft. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b014-v13-05","title":"250 公尺主跨的預製構件體系：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Precast system for the 250 m spans: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「主梁懸臂與中央掛梁」如何影響聯邦大橋（加拿大）的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Main girder cantilevers and drop-ins” governs force, deformation or durability in “Confederation Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主橋段以約 250 公尺的跨徑重複排列，上部結構是後拉預力混凝土箱梁。公開資料指出，主墩、主梁與掛梁都在陸上預製：主梁跨坐在墩頂、向兩側懸臂伸出，相鄰兩支主梁的懸臂端之間再放入一段較短的掛梁，組成完整跨徑。這種體系讓最重的構件在陸上完成，海上只需要放置、對位與連接；但懸臂根部承受極大的負彎矩，必須靠深梁高與大量預力承擔，而掛梁兩端的連接決定了行車平順與伸縮行為。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「主梁懸臂與中央掛梁」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The main bridge repeats spans of about 250 m, with post-tensioned concrete box girders. Public sources state that the main piers, main girders and drop-in spans were all precast on land: a main girder sits astride a pier and cantilevers both ways, and a shorter drop-in span fills the gap between the cantilever tips of adjacent main girders to complete each span. The system keeps the heaviest work on land, leaving placement, alignment and connection at sea; but the cantilever roots carry very large hogging moments that require great depth and heavy prestress, and the drop-in connections govern ride quality and movement behaviour. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Main girder cantilevers and drop-ins” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：主梁每側懸臂 a = 95 m、自重 w = 300 kN/m，懸臂根部彎矩 M = w·a²/2 = 300×95²/2 ≈ 1.35×10⁶ kN·m；60 m 掛梁以 w = 200 kN/m 簡支計，跨中彎矩 M = w·L²/8 = 200×60²/8 = 90,000 kN·m，只約為前者的 1/15。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With 95 m cantilevers each side and self-weight w = 300 kN/m, the root moment is M = w·a²/2 = 300×95²/2 ≈ 1.35×10⁶ kN·m; a 60 m drop-in span at w = 200 kN/m, simply supported, has M = w·L²/8 = 200×60²/8 = 90,000 kN·m, only about 1/15 of the former.","failure":"常見誤解：「預製構件只要在陸上做好，放到墩上就完成了結構體系。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once precast pieces are made on land and set on the piers, the structural system is complete.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「主梁懸臂與中央掛梁」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Main girder cantilevers and drop-ins”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-05-k1","title":"250 公尺主跨的預製構件體系","titleEn":"Precast system for the 250 m spans","text":"主橋段以約 250 公尺的跨徑重複排列，上部結構是後拉預力混凝土箱梁。公開資料指出，主墩、主梁與掛梁都在陸上預製：主梁跨坐在墩頂、向兩側懸臂伸出，相鄰兩支主梁的懸臂端之間再放入一段較短的掛梁，組成完整跨徑。","textEn":"The main bridge repeats spans of about 250 m, with post-tensioned concrete box girders. Public sources state that the main piers, main girders and drop-in spans were all precast on land: a main girder sits astride a pier and cantilevers both ways, and a shorter drop-in span fills the gap between the cantilever tips of adjacent main girders to complete each span.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：預製構件只要在陸上做好，放到墩上就完成了結構體系。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once precast pieces are made on land and set on the piers, the structural system is complete. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「250 公尺主跨的預製構件體系」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Precast system for the 250 m spans\" is correct?","options":["預製構件只要在陸上做好，放到墩上就完成了結構體系。","混凝土強度夠高，就能同時抵抗凍融、氯離子與冰磨蝕。","主橋段以約 250 公尺的跨徑重複排列，上部結構是後拉預力混凝土箱梁。"],"optionsEn":["Once precast pieces are made on land and set on the piers, the structural system is complete.","High concrete strength alone resists freeze–thaw, chlorides and ice abrasion together.","The main bridge repeats spans of about 250 m, with post-tensioned concrete box girders."],"answer":2,"explanation":"主橋段以約 250 公尺的跨徑重複排列，上部結構是後拉預力混凝土箱梁。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The main bridge repeats spans of about 250 m, with post-tensioned concrete box girders. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b014-v13-06","title":"250 公尺主跨的預製構件體系：定量估算","titleEn":"Precast system for the 250 m spans: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「主梁懸臂與中央掛梁」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Main girder cantilevers and drop-ins” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：主梁每側懸臂 a = 95 m、自重 w = 300 kN/m，懸臂根部彎矩 M = w·a²/2 = 300×95²/2 ≈ 1.35×10⁶ kN·m；60 m 掛梁以 w = 200 kN/m 簡支計，跨中彎矩 M = w·L²/8 = 200×60²/8 = 90,000 kN·m，只約為前者的 1/15。尺寸與荷載為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With 95 m cantilevers each side and self-weight w = 300 kN/m, the root moment is M = w·a²/2 = 300×95²/2 ≈ 1.35×10⁶ kN·m; a 60 m drop-in span at w = 200 kN/m, simply supported, has M = w·L²/8 = 200×60²/8 = 90,000 kN·m, only about 1/15 of the former. Dimensions and loads are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以施工階段模型檢查主梁在吊裝、存放與就位時的應力（支點位置不同時彎矩會反轉），並以長期分析預測懸臂端撓度；就位後量測懸臂端高程與掛梁支座位置，確認與預測一致才進行連接。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check main-girder stresses in lifting, storage and placement with a staged model, since moments reverse as support positions change, and predict long-term tip deflections; after placement survey tip levels and drop-in seat positions and connect only when they match predictions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"主梁每側懸臂 a = 95 m、自重 w = 300 kN/m，懸臂根部彎矩 M = w·a²/2 = 300×95²/2 ≈ 1.35×10⁶ kN·m；60 m 掛梁以 w = 200 kN/m 簡支計，跨中彎矩 M = w·L²/8 = 200×60²/8 = 90,000 kN·m，只約為前者的 1/15。尺寸與荷載為教學假設。","textEn":"With 95 m cantilevers each side and self-weight w = 300 kN/m, the root moment is M = w·a²/2 = 300×95²/2 ≈ 1.35×10⁶ kN·m; a 60 m drop-in span at w = 200 kN/m, simply supported, has M = w·L²/8 = 200×60²/8 = 90,000 kN·m, only about 1/15 of the former. Dimensions and loads are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「250 公尺主跨的預製構件體系」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Precast system for the 250 m spans\", which statement holds?","options":["主梁每側懸臂 a = 95 m、自重 w = 300 kN/m，懸臂根部彎矩 M = w·a²/2 = 300×95²/2 ≈ 1.35×10⁶ kN·m。","只要浮吊能力夠大，工程進度就只取決於吊裝速度。","冰力很難量測，所以只能完全依賴設計規範的數值。"],"optionsEn":["With 95 m cantilevers each side and self-weight w = 300 kN/m, the root moment is M = w·a²/2 = 300×95²/2 ≈ 1.35×10⁶ kN·m.","With a big enough crane, progress depends only on lifting speed.","Ice forces cannot be measured, so engineers must rely entirely on code values."],"answer":0,"explanation":"主梁每側懸臂 a = 95 m、自重 w = 300 kN/m，懸臂根部彎矩 M = w·a²/2 = 300×95²/2 ≈ 1.35×10⁶ kN·m；60 m 掛梁以 w = 200 kN/m 簡支計，跨中彎矩 M = w·L²/8 = 200×60²/8 = 90,000 kN·m，只約為前者的 1/15。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With 95 m cantilevers each side and self-weight w = 300 kN/m, the root moment is M = w·a²/2 = 300×95²/2 ≈ 1.35×10⁶ kN·m; a 60 m drop-in span at w = 200 kN/m, simply supported, has M = w·L²/8 = 200×60²/8 = 90,000 kN·m, only about 1/15 of the former. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b014-v13-07","title":"250 公尺主跨的預製構件體系：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Precast system for the 250 m spans: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「主梁懸臂與中央掛梁」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Main girder cantilevers and drop-ins” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以施工階段模型檢查主梁在吊裝、存放與就位時的應力（支點位置不同時彎矩會反轉），並以長期分析預測懸臂端撓度；就位後量測懸臂端高程與掛梁支座位置，確認與預測一致才進行連接。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check main-girder stresses in lifting, storage and placement with a staged model, since moments reverse as support positions change, and predict long-term tip deflections; after placement survey tip levels and drop-in seat positions and connect only when they match predictions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計文件應同時提供每個構件在吊裝、運輸、存放與就位各階段的支承條件與允許應力，並以懸臂端長期撓度預測訂定掛梁座的預留高程；就位與連接順序列為停留點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Design documents should give support conditions and allowable stresses for every component during lifting, transport, storage and placement, and set the drop-in seat levels from long-term tip-deflection predictions; placement and connection sequences are hold points.","failure":"注意干擾：主梁預力或梁高不足時，懸臂根部頂板在長期潛變與活載下開裂；相鄰懸臂端撓度不同時，掛梁兩端產生高差，造成行車跳動與伸縮裝置損壞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Insufficient prestress or depth cracks the top slab at the cantilever root under long-term creep and live load; unequal tip deflections of adjacent cantilevers leave a step at the drop-in ends, causing ride bumps and expansion-device damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以施工階段模型檢查主梁在吊裝、存放與就位時的應力（支點位置不同時彎矩會反轉），並以長期分析預測懸臂端撓度；就位後量測懸臂端高程與掛梁支座位置，確認與預測一致才進行連接。","textEn":"Check main-girder stresses in lifting, storage and placement with a staged model, since moments reverse as support positions change, and predict long-term tip deflections; after placement survey tip levels and drop-in seat positions and connect only when they match predictions.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計文件應同時提供每個構件在吊裝、運輸、存放與就位各階段的支承條件與允許應力，並以懸臂端長期撓度預測訂定掛梁座的預留高程；就位與連接順序列為停留點。","textEn":"Design documents should give support conditions and allowable stresses for every component during lifting, transport, storage and placement, and set the drop-in seat levels from long-term tip-deflection predictions; placement and connection sequences are hold points.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「250 公尺主跨的預製構件體系」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Precast system for the 250 m spans\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以施工階段模型檢查主梁在吊裝、存放與就位時的應力（支點位置不同時彎矩會反轉），並以長期分析預測懸臂端撓度。","鋪面只影響行車舒適，與結構壽命無關。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Check main-girder stresses in lifting, storage and placement with a staged model, since moments reverse as support positions change, and predict long-term tip deflections.","Surfacing only affects ride comfort and has nothing to do with structural life."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以施工階段模型檢查主梁在吊裝、存放與就位時的應力（支點位置不同時彎矩會反轉），並以長期分析預測懸臂端撓度；就位後量測懸臂端高程與掛梁支座位置，確認與預測一致才進行連接。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check main-girder stresses in lifting, storage and placement with a staged model, since moments reverse as support positions change, and predict long-term tip deflections; after placement survey tip levels and drop-in seat positions and connect only when they match predictions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b014-v13-08","title":"250 公尺主跨的預製構件體系：失效診斷","titleEn":"Precast system for the 250 m spans: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「主梁懸臂與中央掛梁」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Main girder cantilevers and drop-ins” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"主梁預力或梁高不足時，懸臂根部頂板在長期潛變與活載下開裂；相鄰懸臂端撓度不同時，掛梁兩端產生高差，造成行車跳動與伸縮裝置損壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Insufficient prestress or depth cracks the top slab at the cantilever root under long-term creep and live load; unequal tip deflections of adjacent cantilevers leave a step at the drop-in ends, causing ride bumps and expansion-device damage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這種體系讓最重的構件在陸上完成，海上只需要放置、對位與連接；但懸臂根部承受極大的負彎矩，必須靠深梁高與大量預力承擔，而掛梁兩端的連接決定了行車平順與伸縮行為。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The system keeps the heaviest work on land, leaving placement, alignment and connection at sea; but the cantilever roots carry very large hogging moments that require great depth and heavy prestress, and the drop-in connections govern ride quality and movement behaviour.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「預製構件只要在陸上做好，放到墩上就完成了結構體系。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once precast pieces are made on land and set on the piers, the structural system is complete.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"主梁預力或梁高不足時，懸臂根部頂板在長期潛變與活載下開裂；相鄰懸臂端撓度不同時，掛梁兩端產生高差，造成行車跳動與伸縮裝置損壞。","textEn":"Insufficient prestress or depth cracks the top slab at the cantilever root under long-term creep and live load; unequal tip deflections of adjacent cantilevers leave a step at the drop-in ends, causing ride bumps and expansion-device damage.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「250 公尺主跨的預製構件體系」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Precast system for the 250 m spans\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","混凝土強度夠高，就能同時抵抗凍融、氯離子與冰磨蝕。","主梁預力或梁高不足時，懸臂根部頂板在長期潛變與活載下開裂；相鄰懸臂端撓度不同時，掛梁兩端產生高差，造成行車跳動與伸縮裝置損壞。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","High concrete strength alone resists freeze–thaw, chlorides and ice abrasion together.","Insufficient prestress or depth cracks the top slab at the cantilever root under long-term creep and live load."],"answer":2,"explanation":"主梁預力或梁高不足時，懸臂根部頂板在長期潛變與活載下開裂；相鄰懸臂端撓度不同時，掛梁兩端產生高差，造成行車跳動與伸縮裝置損壞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Insufficient prestress or depth cracks the top slab at the cantilever root under long-term creep and live load; unequal tip deflections of adjacent cantilevers leave a step at the drop-in ends, causing ride bumps and expansion-device damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b014-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「百年設計壽命的材料選擇」與「預製墩座、墩身與冰盾的接合」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Materials for a 100-year design life\" and \"Joining bases, shafts and ice shields\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b014-v13-09","title":"百年設計壽命的材料選擇：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Materials for a 100-year design life: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「高性能混凝土」如何影響聯邦大橋（加拿大）的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “High-performance concrete” governs force, deformation or durability in “Confederation Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"聯邦大橋的合約要求 100 年設計壽命，約為一般橋梁的兩倍，公開資料指出預製構件使用高等級混凝土與鋼筋來達成。海峽環境同時有三種劣化：海水氯離子讓鋼筋腐蝕、冬季凍融循環讓混凝土表層剝落、浮冰在水線處反覆磨蝕冰盾表面。高性能混凝土以低水膠比與卜作嵐材料降低滲透性，並以適當的氣泡系統抵抗凍融；在冰磨蝕最嚴重的水線帶，常再加大保護層或提高表面耐磨性，把部分厚度當作可犧牲層。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「高性能混凝土」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The contract required a 100-year design life, about twice that of ordinary bridges, and public sources say high-grade concrete and reinforcement in the precast components were used to achieve it. The strait combines three deterioration modes: seawater chlorides corrode reinforcement, winter freeze–thaw cycles scale the concrete surface, and pack ice repeatedly abrades the ice shields at the waterline. High-performance concrete lowers permeability with a low water–binder ratio and pozzolans and resists freeze–thaw with a suitable air-void system; in the waterline band where ice abrasion is worst, cover is often increased or surface abrasion resistance raised, treating part of the thickness as sacrificial. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “High-performance concrete” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：若水線帶冰磨蝕率取 0.5 mm/年，100 年損失 0.5×100 = 50 mm；設計保護層 75 mm 時，只剩約 25 mm 保護鋼筋，因此需要加大保護層或耐磨面層。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If ice abrades the waterline band at 0.5 mm a year, 100 years remove 0.5×100 = 50 mm; with 75 mm cover only about 25 mm would remain over the steel, so larger cover or an abrasion-resistant layer is needed.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度夠高，就能同時抵抗凍融、氯離子與冰磨蝕。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High concrete strength alone resists freeze–thaw, chlorides and ice abrasion together.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「高性能混凝土」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “High-performance concrete”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-09-k1","title":"百年設計壽命的材料選擇","titleEn":"Materials for a 100-year design life","text":"聯邦大橋的合約要求 100 年設計壽命，約為一般橋梁的兩倍，公開資料指出預製構件使用高等級混凝土與鋼筋來達成。海峽環境同時有三種劣化：海水氯離子讓鋼筋腐蝕、冬季凍融循環讓混凝土表層剝落、浮冰在水線處反覆磨蝕冰盾表面。","textEn":"The contract required a 100-year design life, about twice that of ordinary bridges, and public sources say high-grade concrete and reinforcement in the precast components were used to achieve it. The strait combines three deterioration modes: seawater chlorides corrode reinforcement, winter freeze–thaw cycles scale the concrete surface, and pack ice repeatedly abrades the ice shields at the waterline.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度夠高，就能同時抵抗凍融、氯離子與冰磨蝕。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High concrete strength alone resists freeze–thaw, chlorides and ice abrasion together. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「百年設計壽命的材料選擇」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Materials for a 100-year design life\" is correct?","options":["聯邦大橋的合約要求 100 年設計壽命，約為一般橋梁的兩倍，公開資料指出預製構件使用高等級混凝土與鋼筋來達成。","混凝土強度夠高，就能同時抵抗凍融、氯離子與冰磨蝕。","預製構件夠重，疊上去後不需要灌漿或預力就能穩定傳力。"],"optionsEn":["The contract required a 100-year design life, about twice that of ordinary bridges, and public sources say high-grade concrete and reinforcement in the precast components were used to achieve it.","High concrete strength alone resists freeze–thaw, chlorides and ice abrasion together.","Precast pieces are heavy enough to transmit load reliably when stacked, without grout or prestress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"聯邦大橋的合約要求 100 年設計壽命，約為一般橋梁的兩倍，公開資料指出預製構件使用高等級混凝土與鋼筋來達成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The contract required a 100-year design life, about twice that of ordinary bridges, and public sources say high-grade concrete and reinforcement in the precast components were used to achieve it. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b014-v13-10","title":"百年設計壽命的材料選擇：定量估算","titleEn":"Materials for a 100-year design life: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高性能混凝土」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “High-performance concrete” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：若水線帶冰磨蝕率取 0.5 mm/年，100 年損失 0.5×100 = 50 mm；設計保護層 75 mm 時，只剩約 25 mm 保護鋼筋，因此需要加大保護層或耐磨面層。若磨蝕率降為 0.2 mm/年，損失只有 20 mm。磨蝕率與保護層為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If ice abrades the waterline band at 0.5 mm a year, 100 years remove 0.5×100 = 50 mm; with 75 mm cover only about 25 mm would remain over the steel, so larger cover or an abrasion-resistant layer is needed. At 0.2 mm a year the loss is only 20 mm. Abrasion rates and cover are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：配比驗證包含抗壓強度、氯離子滲透、凍融耐久（例如 ASTM C666）與氣泡間距係數；預製場逐批抽驗並保存試驗紀錄；營運期在水線帶定期量測磨蝕深度與保護層剩餘厚度，建立劣化速率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mix qualification includes compressive strength, chloride penetration, freeze–thaw durability (for example ASTM C666) and air-void spacing factor; the casting yard tests every batch and keeps records; in service the waterline band is measured periodically for abrasion depth and remaining cover to establish deterioration rates.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"若水線帶冰磨蝕率取 0.5 mm/年，100 年損失 0.5×100 = 50 mm；設計保護層 75 mm 時，只剩約 25 mm 保護鋼筋，因此需要加大保護層或耐磨面層。若磨蝕率降為 0.2 mm/年，損失只有 20 mm。磨蝕率與保護層為教學假設。","textEn":"If ice abrades the waterline band at 0.5 mm a year, 100 years remove 0.5×100 = 50 mm; with 75 mm cover only about 25 mm would remain over the steel, so larger cover or an abrasion-resistant layer is needed. At 0.2 mm a year the loss is only 20 mm. Abrasion rates and cover are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「百年設計壽命的材料選擇」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Materials for a 100-year design life\", which statement holds?","options":["預製構件尺寸精準，放上去後的高程就不會再改變。","若水線帶冰磨蝕率取 0.5 mm/年，100 年損失 0.5×100 = 50 mm。","只要橋梁結構能承受颱風等級的風，車輛在橋上就一定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Precast pieces are accurate, so their levels stay fixed after placement.","If ice abrades the waterline band at 0.5 mm a year, 100 years remove 0.5×100 = 50 mm.","If the structure can withstand storm winds, vehicles on it are automatically safe."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若水線帶冰磨蝕率取 0.5 mm/年，100 年損失 0.5×100 = 50 mm；設計保護層 75 mm 時，只剩約 25 mm 保護鋼筋，因此需要加大保護層或耐磨面層。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If ice abrades the waterline band at 0.5 mm a year, 100 years remove 0.5×100 = 50 mm; with 75 mm cover only about 25 mm would remain over the steel, so larger cover or an abrasion-resistant layer is needed. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b014-v13-11","title":"百年設計壽命的材料選擇：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Materials for a 100-year design life: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高性能混凝土」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “High-performance concrete” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"配比驗證包含抗壓強度、氯離子滲透、凍融耐久（例如 ASTM C666）與氣泡間距係數；預製場逐批抽驗並保存試驗紀錄；營運期在水線帶定期量測磨蝕深度與保護層剩餘厚度，建立劣化速率。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mix qualification includes compressive strength, chloride penetration, freeze–thaw durability (for example ASTM C666) and air-void spacing factor; the casting yard tests every batch and keeps records; in service the waterline band is measured periodically for abrasion depth and remaining cover to establish deterioration rates. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：耐久規範應依暴露區（水下、潮汐、浪濺、水線冰磨、橋面）分別訂定保護層、配比與試驗要求，預製場的品質紀錄須逐構件追溯；在水線帶預設量測點，作為日後磨蝕評估的基準。","observationEn":"Site practice: The durability specification should set cover, mix and test requirements by exposure zone (submerged, tidal, splash, waterline ice abrasion, deck), with yard quality records traceable to each component; reference points in the waterline band provide a baseline for future abrasion surveys.","failure":"注意干擾：若混凝土氣泡系統不足，凍融循環使表層逐年剝落，保護層變薄、氯離子更快到達鋼筋；水線帶磨蝕若未監測，數十年後鋼筋外露，修補必須在冰季以外的短窗口進行，代價很高。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A deficient air-void system lets freeze–thaw scale the surface year by year, thinning cover so chlorides reach the steel sooner; unmonitored waterline abrasion can expose reinforcement after decades, and repairs must fit short windows outside the ice season at great cost. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"配比驗證包含抗壓強度、氯離子滲透、凍融耐久（例如 ASTM C666）與氣泡間距係數；預製場逐批抽驗並保存試驗紀錄；營運期在水線帶定期量測磨蝕深度與保護層剩餘厚度，建立劣化速率。","textEn":"Mix qualification includes compressive strength, chloride penetration, freeze–thaw durability (for example ASTM C666) and air-void spacing factor; the casting yard tests every batch and keeps records; in service the waterline band is measured periodically for abrasion depth and remaining cover to establish deterioration rates.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"耐久規範應依暴露區（水下、潮汐、浪濺、水線冰磨、橋面）分別訂定保護層、配比與試驗要求，預製場的品質紀錄須逐構件追溯；在水線帶預設量測點，作為日後磨蝕評估的基準。","textEn":"The durability specification should set cover, mix and test requirements by exposure zone (submerged, tidal, splash, waterline ice abrasion, deck), with yard quality records traceable to each component; reference points in the waterline band provide a baseline for future abrasion surveys.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「百年設計壽命的材料選擇」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Materials for a 100-year design life\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","特許期結束時橋還能通車，就代表結構狀態良好。","配比驗證包含抗壓強度、氯離子滲透、凍融耐久（例如 ASTM C666）與氣泡間距係數。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","If the bridge is still open at the end of the concession, its condition must be good.","Mix qualification includes compressive strength, chloride penetration, freeze–thaw durability (for example ASTM C666) and air-void spacing factor."],"answer":2,"explanation":"配比驗證包含抗壓強度、氯離子滲透、凍融耐久（例如 ASTM C666）與氣泡間距係數；預製場逐批抽驗並保存試驗紀錄；營運期在水線帶定期量測磨蝕深度與保護層剩餘厚度，建立劣化速率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mix qualification includes compressive strength, chloride penetration, freeze–thaw durability (for example ASTM C666) and air-void spacing factor; the casting yard tests every batch and keeps records; in service the waterline band is measured periodically for abrasion depth and remaining cover to establish deterioration rates. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b014-v13-12","title":"百年設計壽命的材料選擇：失效診斷","titleEn":"Materials for a 100-year design life: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高性能混凝土」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “High-performance concrete” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若混凝土氣泡系統不足，凍融循環使表層逐年剝落，保護層變薄、氯離子更快到達鋼筋；水線帶磨蝕若未監測，數十年後鋼筋外露，修補必須在冰季以外的短窗口進行，代價很高。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A deficient air-void system lets freeze–thaw scale the surface year by year, thinning cover so chlorides reach the steel sooner; unmonitored waterline abrasion can expose reinforcement after decades, and repairs must fit short windows outside the ice season at great cost. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：高性能混凝土以低水膠比與卜作嵐材料降低滲透性，並以適當的氣泡系統抵抗凍融；在冰磨蝕最嚴重的水線帶，常再加大保護層或提高表面耐磨性，把部分厚度當作可犧牲層。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: High-performance concrete lowers permeability with a low water–binder ratio and pozzolans and resists freeze–thaw with a suitable air-void system; in the waterline band where ice abrasion is worst, cover is often increased or surface abrasion resistance raised, treating part of the thickness as sacrificial.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度夠高，就能同時抵抗凍融、氯離子與冰磨蝕。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High concrete strength alone resists freeze–thaw, chlorides and ice abrasion together.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若混凝土氣泡系統不足，凍融循環使表層逐年剝落，保護層變薄、氯離子更快到達鋼筋；水線帶磨蝕若未監測，數十年後鋼筋外露，修補必須在冰季以外的短窗口進行，代價很高。","textEn":"A deficient air-void system lets freeze–thaw scale the surface year by year, thinning cover so chlorides reach the steel sooner; unmonitored waterline abrasion can expose reinforcement after decades, and repairs must fit short windows outside the ice season at great cost.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「百年設計壽命的材料選擇」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Materials for a 100-year design life\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若混凝土氣泡系統不足，凍融循環使表層逐年剝落，保護層變薄、氯離子更快到達鋼筋；水線帶磨蝕若未監測，數十年後鋼筋外露，修補必須在冰季以外的短窗口進行，代價很高。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","預製構件夠重，疊上去後不需要灌漿或預力就能穩定傳力。"],"optionsEn":["A deficient air-void system lets freeze–thaw scale the surface year by year, thinning cover so chlorides reach the steel sooner.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Precast pieces are heavy enough to transmit load reliably when stacked, without grout or prestress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若混凝土氣泡系統不足，凍融循環使表層逐年剝落，保護層變薄、氯離子更快到達鋼筋；水線帶磨蝕若未監測，數十年後鋼筋外露，修補必須在冰季以外的短窗口進行，代價很高。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A deficient air-void system lets freeze–thaw scale the surface year by year, thinning cover so chlorides reach the steel sooner; unmonitored waterline abrasion can expose reinforcement after decades, and repairs must fit short windows outside the ice season at great cost. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b014-v13-13","title":"預製墩座、墩身與冰盾的接合：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Joining bases, shafts and ice shields: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「墩座與墩身接合面」如何影響聯邦大橋（加拿大）的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pier base-to-shaft joint” governs force, deformation or durability in “Confederation Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"每座主墩由多個大型預製件組成：坐在海床上的墩座、帶有冰盾的墩身，以及上方的主梁。構件之間的接合面必須同時傳遞巨大的垂直力、冰與風造成的水平力和彎矩，通常以灌漿填平接觸面，再以後拉預力把構件壓成一體。灌漿層讓不完全平整的接觸面均勻受力，預力則讓接合面在設計荷載下維持受壓、不張開，否則海水會進入接縫腐蝕預力鋼材。接合面的摩擦抗剪也是抵抗浮冰水平推力的主要機制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「墩座與墩身接合面」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each main pier is assembled from large precast pieces: a base seated on the seabed, a shaft carrying the ice shield, and the main girder above. Joints between them must transmit huge vertical loads together with horizontal forces and moments from ice and wind, typically by grouting the contact faces and post-tensioning the pieces together. The grout layer spreads load over imperfect contact surfaces, and prestress keeps the joint in compression under design loads so it does not open, otherwise seawater would enter and corrode the tendons. Friction across the joint is also the main mechanism resisting horizontal ice thrust. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Pier base-to-shaft joint” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：剪力摩擦 V_cap = μ·N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Shear friction V_cap = μ·N.","failure":"常見誤解：「預製構件夠重，疊上去後不需要灌漿或預力就能穩定傳力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Precast pieces are heavy enough to transmit load reliably when stacked, without grout or prestress.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「墩座與墩身接合面」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Pier base-to-shaft joint”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-13-k1","title":"預製墩座、墩身與冰盾的接合","titleEn":"Joining bases, shafts and ice shields","text":"每座主墩由多個大型預製件組成：坐在海床上的墩座、帶有冰盾的墩身，以及上方的主梁。構件之間的接合面必須同時傳遞巨大的垂直力、冰與風造成的水平力和彎矩，通常以灌漿填平接觸面，再以後拉預力把構件壓成一體。","textEn":"Each main pier is assembled from large precast pieces: a base seated on the seabed, a shaft carrying the ice shield, and the main girder above. Joints between them must transmit huge vertical loads together with horizontal forces and moments from ice and wind, typically by grouting the contact faces and post-tensioning the pieces together.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：預製構件夠重，疊上去後不需要灌漿或預力就能穩定傳力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Precast pieces are heavy enough to transmit load reliably when stacked, without grout or prestress. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「預製墩座、墩身與冰盾的接合」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joining bases, shafts and ice shields\" is correct?","options":["預製構件夠重，疊上去後不需要灌漿或預力就能穩定傳力。","每座主墩由多個大型預製件組成：坐在海床上的墩座、帶有冰盾的墩身，以及上方的主梁。","只要浮吊能力夠大，工程進度就只取決於吊裝速度。"],"optionsEn":["Precast pieces are heavy enough to transmit load reliably when stacked, without grout or prestress.","Each main pier is assembled from large precast pieces: a base seated on the seabed, a shaft carrying the ice shield, and the main girder above.","With a big enough crane, progress depends only on lifting speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每座主墩由多個大型預製件組成：坐在海床上的墩座、帶有冰盾的墩身，以及上方的主梁。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each main pier is assembled from large precast pieces: a base seated on the seabed, a shaft carrying the ice shield, and the main girder above. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b014-v13-14","title":"預製墩座、墩身與冰盾的接合：定量估算","titleEn":"Joining bases, shafts and ice shields: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「墩座與墩身接合面」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pier base-to-shaft joint” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：剪力摩擦 V_cap = μ·N。若接合面上方承受主梁重 7,500 t（N = 7,500×9.81 ≈ 73,600 kN）、摩擦係數 μ = 0.6，V_cap ≈ 0.6×73,600 ≈ 44,100 kN，遠大於錐面冰力 2.52 MN，也大於垂直面壓碎力 16.8 MN。重量與 μ 為教學假設；實際設計還需加上預力與抗剪鍵。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Shear friction V_cap = μ·N. With a 7,500 t main girder above the joint (N = 7,500×9.81 ≈ 73,600 kN) and μ = 0.6, V_cap ≈ 0.6×73,600 ≈ 44,100 kN, far above the 2.52 MN cone ice force and also above the 16.8 MN crushing force. Weight and μ are teaching assumptions; real design also adds prestress and shear keys. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：構件就位後以 GNSS 與全站儀量測平面位置、高程與垂直度，公開資料指出定位精度可達約 2 cm；灌漿時記錄灌入量與壓力並確認溢漿，預力張拉逐束記錄伸長量與油壓，與計算比較；接縫以目視與潛水檢查確認無漏漿與張開。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After placement survey plan position, level and plumb by GNSS and total station, with public sources citing placement to about 2 cm; during grouting record volume and pressure and confirm vent overflow; record elongation and jack pressure for each tendon against calculation; inspect joints visually and by divers for grout leaks or opening.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"剪力摩擦 V_cap = μ·N。若接合面上方承受主梁重 7,500 t（N = 7,500×9.81 ≈ 73,600 kN）、摩擦係數 μ = 0.6，V_cap ≈ 0.6×73,600 ≈ 44,100 kN，遠大於錐面冰力 2.52 MN，也大於垂直面壓碎力 16.8 MN。重量與 μ 為教學假設；實際設計還需加上預力與抗剪鍵。","textEn":"Shear friction V_cap = μ·N. With a 7,500 t main girder above the joint (N = 7,500×9.81 ≈ 73,600 kN) and μ = 0.6, V_cap ≈ 0.6×73,600 ≈ 44,100 kN, far above the 2.52 MN cone ice force and also above the 16.8 MN crushing force. Weight and μ are teaching assumptions; real design also adds prestress and shear keys.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「預製墩座、墩身與冰盾的接合」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joining bases, shafts and ice shields\", which statement holds?","options":["冰力很難量測，所以只能完全依賴設計規範的數值。","鋪面只影響行車舒適，與結構壽命無關。","剪力摩擦 V_cap = μ·N。"],"optionsEn":["Ice forces cannot be measured, so engineers must rely entirely on code values.","Surfacing only affects ride comfort and has nothing to do with structural life.","Shear friction V_cap = μ·N."],"answer":2,"explanation":"剪力摩擦 V_cap = μ·N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Shear friction V_cap = μ·N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b014-v13-15","title":"預製墩座、墩身與冰盾的接合：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joining bases, shafts and ice shields: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「墩座與墩身接合面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pier base-to-shaft joint” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"構件就位後以 GNSS 與全站儀量測平面位置、高程與垂直度，公開資料指出定位精度可達約 2 cm；灌漿時記錄灌入量與壓力並確認溢漿，預力張拉逐束記錄伸長量與油壓，與計算比較；接縫以目視與潛水檢查確認無漏漿與張開。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After placement survey plan position, level and plumb by GNSS and total station, with public sources citing placement to about 2 cm; during grouting record volume and pressure and confirm vent overflow; record elongation and jack pressure for each tendon against calculation; inspect joints visually and by divers for grout leaks or opening. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：接合程序應依序設停留點：接觸面清潔與量測、灌漿與溢漿確認、預力張拉與紀錄、孔道灌漿與封錨；每個接縫建立紀錄卡，交接時納入營運資料，作為日後檢查預力狀態的依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: The joining procedure should have sequential hold points: surface cleaning and survey, grouting with vent confirmation, tendon stressing with records, duct grouting and anchor sealing; every joint gets a record card that enters the operating file as the basis for later checks of tendon condition.","failure":"注意干擾：接觸面灌漿不完整時，荷載集中在少數接觸點，局部壓碎並在預力作用下產生裂縫；預力損失或接縫張開讓海水進入孔道，預力鋼材腐蝕而無法目視發現，是預製海事結構最危險的隱蔽劣化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Incomplete joint grouting concentrates load on a few contact points, crushing them locally and cracking under prestress; prestress loss or joint opening lets seawater into ducts and corrodes tendons invisibly, the most dangerous hidden deterioration in precast marine structures. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"構件就位後以 GNSS 與全站儀量測平面位置、高程與垂直度，公開資料指出定位精度可達約 2 cm；灌漿時記錄灌入量與壓力並確認溢漿，預力張拉逐束記錄伸長量與油壓，與計算比較；接縫以目視與潛水檢查確認無漏漿與張開。","textEn":"After placement survey plan position, level and plumb by GNSS and total station, with public sources citing placement to about 2 cm; during grouting record volume and pressure and confirm vent overflow; record elongation and jack pressure for each tendon against calculation; inspect joints visually and by divers for grout leaks or opening.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"接合程序應依序設停留點：接觸面清潔與量測、灌漿與溢漿確認、預力張拉與紀錄、孔道灌漿與封錨；每個接縫建立紀錄卡，交接時納入營運資料，作為日後檢查預力狀態的依據。","textEn":"The joining procedure should have sequential hold points: surface cleaning and survey, grouting with vent confirmation, tendon stressing with records, duct grouting and anchor sealing; every joint gets a record card that enters the operating file as the basis for later checks of tendon condition.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「預製墩座、墩身與冰盾的接合」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joining bases, shafts and ice shields\"?","options":["構件就位後以 GNSS 與全站儀量測平面位置、高程與垂直度，公開資料指出定位精度可達約 2 cm。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","冰比混凝土軟得多，所以浮冰對橋墩的力量可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["After placement survey plan position, level and plumb by GNSS and total station, with public sources citing placement to about 2 cm.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Ice is much softer than concrete, so pack-ice forces on piers are negligible."],"answer":0,"explanation":"構件就位後以 GNSS 與全站儀量測平面位置、高程與垂直度，公開資料指出定位精度可達約 2 cm；灌漿時記錄灌入量與壓力並確認溢漿，預力張拉逐束記錄伸長量與油壓，與計算比較；接縫以目視與潛水檢查確認無漏漿與張開。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After placement survey plan position, level and plumb by GNSS and total station, with public sources citing placement to about 2 cm; during grouting record volume and pressure and confirm vent overflow; record elongation and jack pressure for each tendon against calculation; inspect joints visually and by divers for grout leaks or opening. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b014-v13-16","title":"預製墩座、墩身與冰盾的接合：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joining bases, shafts and ice shields: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「墩座與墩身接合面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pier base-to-shaft joint” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接觸面灌漿不完整時，荷載集中在少數接觸點，局部壓碎並在預力作用下產生裂縫；預力損失或接縫張開讓海水進入孔道，預力鋼材腐蝕而無法目視發現，是預製海事結構最危險的隱蔽劣化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Incomplete joint grouting concentrates load on a few contact points, crushing them locally and cracking under prestress; prestress loss or joint opening lets seawater into ducts and corrodes tendons invisibly, the most dangerous hidden deterioration in precast marine structures. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：接合面的摩擦抗剪也是抵抗浮冰水平推力的主要機制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Friction across the joint is also the main mechanism resisting horizontal ice thrust.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「預製構件夠重，疊上去後不需要灌漿或預力就能穩定傳力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Precast pieces are heavy enough to transmit load reliably when stacked, without grout or prestress.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接觸面灌漿不完整時，荷載集中在少數接觸點，局部壓碎並在預力作用下產生裂縫；預力損失或接縫張開讓海水進入孔道，預力鋼材腐蝕而無法目視發現，是預製海事結構最危險的隱蔽劣化。","textEn":"Incomplete joint grouting concentrates load on a few contact points, crushing them locally and cracking under prestress; prestress loss or joint opening lets seawater into ducts and corrodes tendons invisibly, the most dangerous hidden deterioration in precast marine structures.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「預製墩座、墩身與冰盾的接合」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joining bases, shafts and ice shields\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","接觸面灌漿不完整時，荷載集中在少數接觸點，局部壓碎並在預力作用下產生裂縫。","只要浮吊能力夠大，工程進度就只取決於吊裝速度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Incomplete joint grouting concentrates load on a few contact points, crushing them locally and cracking under prestress.","With a big enough crane, progress depends only on lifting speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸面灌漿不完整時，荷載集中在少數接觸點，局部壓碎並在預力作用下產生裂縫；預力損失或接縫張開讓海水進入孔道，預力鋼材腐蝕而無法目視發現，是預製海事結構最危險的隱蔽劣化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Incomplete joint grouting concentrates load on a few contact points, crushing them locally and cracking under prestress; prestress loss or joint opening lets seawater into ducts and corrodes tendons invisibly, the most dangerous hidden deterioration in precast marine structures. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b014-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「預製場、Svanen 與每週一跨」與「主梁就位、掛梁與線形控制」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"The casting yard, Svanen and a span a week\" and \"Girder placement, drop-ins and alignment\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b014-v13-17","title":"預製場、Svanen 與每週一跨：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"The casting yard, Svanen and a span a week: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「陸上預製場與重件運輸」如何影響聯邦大橋（加拿大）的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Land casting yard and heavy transport” governs force, deformation or durability in “Confederation Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主墩、主梁與掛梁都在愛德華王子島博登—卡爾頓附近的預製場製作，構件在場內以履帶式運輸車沿軌道移動到存放區與碼頭，再由浮吊 Svanen 運到海上吊放。公開資料提到全橋約有 175 件主要構件，最重約 7,500 公噸，高峰期每週可完成一跨。把海上工作化為陸上工廠作業，品質與進度較能掌控，但整個工程的節奏取決於預製場產能、存放空間、浮吊與海況，以及每年冰季前必須完成的安裝窗口。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「陸上預製場與重件運輸」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The main piers, main girders and drop-in spans were made at a casting yard near Borden-Carleton, Prince Edward Island, moved within the yard by crawler transporters on rails to storage and the wharf, and then carried out and placed by the floating crane Svanen. Public sources mention about 175 major structural pieces, the heaviest about 7,500 t, with one span completed each week at the peak. Turning marine work into a land factory improves control of quality and schedule, but the pace of the whole job depends on yard output, storage space, the crane, sea conditions and the installation window that must close before each ice season. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Land casting yard and heavy transport” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：主橋 44 跨、每跨約 4 件主要構件（墩座、墩身、主梁、掛梁），共約 44×4 = 176 件，與公開的約 175 件相符。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With 44 main spans and about 4 major pieces each (base, shaft, main girder, drop-in), there are about 44×4 = 176 pieces, consistent with the published figure of about 175.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要浮吊能力夠大，工程進度就只取決於吊裝速度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With a big enough crane, progress depends only on lifting speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「陸上預製場與重件運輸」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Land casting yard and heavy transport”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-17-k1","title":"預製場、Svanen 與每週一跨","titleEn":"The casting yard, Svanen and a span a week","text":"主墩、主梁與掛梁都在愛德華王子島博登—卡爾頓附近的預製場製作，構件在場內以履帶式運輸車沿軌道移動到存放區與碼頭，再由浮吊 Svanen 運到海上吊放。公開資料提到全橋約有 175 件主要構件，最重約 7,500 公噸，高峰期每週可完成一跨。","textEn":"The main piers, main girders and drop-in spans were made at a casting yard near Borden-Carleton, Prince Edward Island, moved within the yard by crawler transporters on rails to storage and the wharf, and then carried out and placed by the floating crane Svanen. Public sources mention about 175 major structural pieces, the heaviest about 7,500 t, with one span completed each week at the peak.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要浮吊能力夠大，工程進度就只取決於吊裝速度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With a big enough crane, progress depends only on lifting speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「預製場、Svanen 與每週一跨」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"The casting yard, Svanen and a span a week\" is correct?","options":["只要浮吊能力夠大，工程進度就只取決於吊裝速度。","預製構件尺寸精準，放上去後的高程就不會再改變。","主墩、主梁與掛梁都在愛德華王子島博登—卡爾頓附近的預製場製作，構件在場內以履帶式運輸車沿軌道移動到存放區與碼頭，再由浮吊 Svanen 運到海上吊放。"],"optionsEn":["With a big enough crane, progress depends only on lifting speed.","Precast pieces are accurate, so their levels stay fixed after placement.","The main piers, main girders and drop-in spans were made at a casting yard near Borden-Carleton, Prince Edward Island, moved within the yard by crawler transporters on rails to storage and the wharf, and then carried out and placed by the floating crane Svanen."],"answer":2,"explanation":"主墩、主梁與掛梁都在愛德華王子島博登—卡爾頓附近的預製場製作，構件在場內以履帶式運輸車沿軌道移動到存放區與碼頭，再由浮吊 Svanen 運到海上吊放。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The main piers, main girders and drop-in spans were made at a casting yard near Borden-Carleton, Prince Edward Island, moved within the yard by crawler transporters on rails to storage and the wharf, and then carried out and placed by the floating crane Svanen. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b014-v13-18","title":"預製場、Svanen 與每週一跨：定量估算","titleEn":"The casting yard, Svanen and a span a week: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「陸上預製場與重件運輸」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Land casting yard and heavy transport” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：主橋 44 跨、每跨約 4 件主要構件（墩座、墩身、主梁、掛梁），共約 44×4 = 176 件，與公開的約 175 件相符。若兩個無冰施工季各 30 週、共 60 週，平均每週需完成 44/60 ≈ 0.73 跨；高峰期每週一跨表示每週約 4 次重件吊放。每跨構件數與施工週數為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With 44 main spans and about 4 major pieces each (base, shaft, main girder, drop-in), there are about 44×4 = 176 pieces, consistent with the published figure of about 175. If two ice-free seasons of 30 weeks each give 60 weeks, the average rate must be 44/60 ≈ 0.73 spans a week; a peak of one span a week means about 4 heavy lifts a week. Pieces per span and season length are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以預製、存放、運輸與吊放的排程模擬檢查產能瓶頸；每件構件出場前檢查強度、尺寸、預埋件與吊點，並秤重確認；每次吊放前依海象預報確認浪高、風速與冰況，吊放後量測位置並記錄，作為下一件構件的修正依據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Simulate the schedule of casting, storage, transport and lifting to find bottlenecks; before each piece leaves the yard check strength, dimensions, embedded items and lifting points and weigh it; before each lift confirm wave, wind and ice forecasts, then survey and record the placed position as the correction basis for the next piece.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"主橋 44 跨、每跨約 4 件主要構件（墩座、墩身、主梁、掛梁），共約 44×4 = 176 件，與公開的約 175 件相符。若兩個無冰施工季各 30 週、共 60 週，平均每週需完成 44/60 ≈ 0.73 跨；高峰期每週一跨表示每週約 4 次重件吊放。每跨構件數與施工週數為教學假設。","textEn":"With 44 main spans and about 4 major pieces each (base, shaft, main girder, drop-in), there are about 44×4 = 176 pieces, consistent with the published figure of about 175. If two ice-free seasons of 30 weeks each give 60 weeks, the average rate must be 44/60 ≈ 0.73 spans a week; a peak of one span a week means about 4 heavy lifts a week. Pieces per span and season length are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「預製場、Svanen 與每週一跨」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"The casting yard, Svanen and a span a week\", which statement holds?","options":["主橋 44 跨、每跨約 4 件主要構件（墩座、墩身、主梁、掛梁），共約 44×4 = 176 件，與公開的約 175 件相符。","只要橋梁結構能承受颱風等級的風，車輛在橋上就一定安全。","特許期結束時橋還能通車，就代表結構狀態良好。"],"optionsEn":["With 44 main spans and about 4 major pieces each (base, shaft, main girder, drop-in), there are about 44×4 = 176 pieces, consistent with the published figure of about 175.","If the structure can withstand storm winds, vehicles on it are automatically safe.","If the bridge is still open at the end of the concession, its condition must be good."],"answer":0,"explanation":"主橋 44 跨、每跨約 4 件主要構件（墩座、墩身、主梁、掛梁），共約 44×4 = 176 件，與公開的約 175 件相符。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With 44 main spans and about 4 major pieces each (base, shaft, main girder, drop-in), there are about 44×4 = 176 pieces, consistent with the published figure of about 175. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b014-v13-19","title":"預製場、Svanen 與每週一跨：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"The casting yard, Svanen and a span a week: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「陸上預製場與重件運輸」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Land casting yard and heavy transport” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以預製、存放、運輸與吊放的排程模擬檢查產能瓶頸；每件構件出場前檢查強度、尺寸、預埋件與吊點，並秤重確認；每次吊放前依海象預報確認浪高、風速與冰況，吊放後量測位置並記錄，作為下一件構件的修正依據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Simulate the schedule of casting, storage, transport and lifting to find bottlenecks; before each piece leaves the yard check strength, dimensions, embedded items and lifting points and weigh it; before each lift confirm wave, wind and ice forecasts, then survey and record the placed position as the correction basis for the next piece. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：整體施工計畫應以冰季為硬性約束，訂定每季必須完成的墩位與越冬安全狀態；預製場與海上作業共用一套構件追蹤系統，記錄每件的製造、檢驗、存放與安裝資料，交接時完整移交。","observationEn":"Site practice: The overall programme should treat the ice season as a hard constraint, fixing which piers must be complete each season and the safe overwintering state; yard and marine operations share one component-tracking system recording fabrication, inspection, storage and installation of every piece, handed over in full.","failure":"注意干擾：預製場進度落後時，安裝被推遲到秋末，冰季提前來臨使部分墩位暴露在未完成狀態下過冬；重件在存放區支承不當時，構件可能在吊裝前就出現裂縫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the yard falls behind, installation slips into late autumn and an early ice season leaves some piers to winter in an unfinished state; heavy pieces stored on poorly placed supports can crack before they are ever lifted. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以預製、存放、運輸與吊放的排程模擬檢查產能瓶頸；每件構件出場前檢查強度、尺寸、預埋件與吊點，並秤重確認；每次吊放前依海象預報確認浪高、風速與冰況，吊放後量測位置並記錄，作為下一件構件的修正依據。","textEn":"Simulate the schedule of casting, storage, transport and lifting to find bottlenecks; before each piece leaves the yard check strength, dimensions, embedded items and lifting points and weigh it; before each lift confirm wave, wind and ice forecasts, then survey and record the placed position as the correction basis for the next piece.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"整體施工計畫應以冰季為硬性約束，訂定每季必須完成的墩位與越冬安全狀態；預製場與海上作業共用一套構件追蹤系統，記錄每件的製造、檢驗、存放與安裝資料，交接時完整移交。","textEn":"The overall programme should treat the ice season as a hard constraint, fixing which piers must be complete each season and the safe overwintering state; yard and marine operations share one component-tracking system recording fabrication, inspection, storage and installation of every piece, handed over in full.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「預製場、Svanen 與每週一跨」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"The casting yard, Svanen and a span a week\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以預製、存放、運輸與吊放的排程模擬檢查產能瓶頸。","預製構件只要在陸上做好，放到墩上就完成了結構體系。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Simulate the schedule of casting, storage, transport and lifting to find bottlenecks.","Once precast pieces are made on land and set on the piers, the structural system is complete."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以預製、存放、運輸與吊放的排程模擬檢查產能瓶頸；每件構件出場前檢查強度、尺寸、預埋件與吊點，並秤重確認；每次吊放前依海象預報確認浪高、風速與冰況，吊放後量測位置並記錄，作為下一件構件的修正依據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Simulate the schedule of casting, storage, transport and lifting to find bottlenecks; before each piece leaves the yard check strength, dimensions, embedded items and lifting points and weigh it; before each lift confirm wave, wind and ice forecasts, then survey and record the placed position as the correction basis for the next piece. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b014-v13-20","title":"預製場、Svanen 與每週一跨：失效診斷","titleEn":"The casting yard, Svanen and a span a week: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「陸上預製場與重件運輸」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Land casting yard and heavy transport” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"預製場進度落後時，安裝被推遲到秋末，冰季提前來臨使部分墩位暴露在未完成狀態下過冬；重件在存放區支承不當時，構件可能在吊裝前就出現裂縫。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the yard falls behind, installation slips into late autumn and an early ice season leaves some piers to winter in an unfinished state; heavy pieces stored on poorly placed supports can crack before they are ever lifted. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把海上工作化為陸上工廠作業，品質與進度較能掌控，但整個工程的節奏取決於預製場產能、存放空間、浮吊與海況，以及每年冰季前必須完成的安裝窗口。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Turning marine work into a land factory improves control of quality and schedule, but the pace of the whole job depends on yard output, storage space, the crane, sea conditions and the installation window that must close before each ice season.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要浮吊能力夠大，工程進度就只取決於吊裝速度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With a big enough crane, progress depends only on lifting speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"預製場進度落後時，安裝被推遲到秋末，冰季提前來臨使部分墩位暴露在未完成狀態下過冬；重件在存放區支承不當時，構件可能在吊裝前就出現裂縫。","textEn":"If the yard falls behind, installation slips into late autumn and an early ice season leaves some piers to winter in an unfinished state; heavy pieces stored on poorly placed supports can crack before they are ever lifted.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「預製場、Svanen 與每週一跨」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"The casting yard, Svanen and a span a week\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","預製構件尺寸精準，放上去後的高程就不會再改變。","預製場進度落後時，安裝被推遲到秋末，冰季提前來臨使部分墩位暴露在未完成狀態下過冬；重件在存放區支承不當時，構件可能在吊裝前就出現裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Precast pieces are accurate, so their levels stay fixed after placement.","If the yard falls behind, installation slips into late autumn and an early ice season leaves some piers to winter in an unfinished state."],"answer":2,"explanation":"預製場進度落後時，安裝被推遲到秋末，冰季提前來臨使部分墩位暴露在未完成狀態下過冬；重件在存放區支承不當時，構件可能在吊裝前就出現裂縫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the yard falls behind, installation slips into late autumn and an early ice season leaves some piers to winter in an unfinished state; heavy pieces stored on poorly placed supports can crack before they are ever lifted. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b014-v13-21","title":"主梁就位、掛梁與線形控制：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Girder placement, drop-ins and alignment: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「掛梁就位與懸臂端高差」如何影響聯邦大橋（加拿大）的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drop-in seating and tip level difference” governs force, deformation or durability in “Confederation Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主梁放上墩頂後，兩側懸臂端會在自重與預力作用下產生撓度，並隨混凝土潛變與收縮持續變化；掛梁放入時，兩端支座的高程取決於相鄰兩支主梁的懸臂端撓度。如果相鄰主梁的製造齡期、預力或放置時間不同，兩者的潛變速率不同，掛梁兩端就會出現高差。線形控制因此必須以時間為變數：預測每支主梁在放置掛梁時與長期的撓度，調整掛梁座高程或墊片，讓完工後的橋面縱斷面平順。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「掛梁就位與懸臂端高差」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Once a main girder is set on its pier, both cantilever tips deflect under self-weight and prestress and keep moving with creep and shrinkage; when a drop-in is placed, its seat levels depend on the tip deflections of the two neighbouring main girders. If those girders differ in casting age, prestress or placement date, their creep rates differ and the drop-in ends end up at different levels. Alignment control must therefore treat time as a variable: predict each girder's deflection at drop-in placement and in the long term, and adjust seat levels or shims so the finished profile is smooth. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Drop-in seating and tip level difference” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：懸臂端彈性撓度 40 mm，長期撓度 ≈ δ_el·(1+φ)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Elastic tip deflection is 40 mm and long-term deflection ≈ δ_el·(1+φ).","failure":"常見誤解：「預製構件尺寸精準，放上去後的高程就不會再改變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Precast pieces are accurate, so their levels stay fixed after placement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「掛梁就位與懸臂端高差」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Drop-in seating and tip level difference”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-21-k1","title":"主梁就位、掛梁與線形控制","titleEn":"Girder placement, drop-ins and alignment","text":"主梁放上墩頂後，兩側懸臂端會在自重與預力作用下產生撓度，並隨混凝土潛變與收縮持續變化；掛梁放入時，兩端支座的高程取決於相鄰兩支主梁的懸臂端撓度。如果相鄰主梁的製造齡期、預力或放置時間不同，兩者的潛變速率不同，掛梁兩端就會出現高差。","textEn":"Once a main girder is set on its pier, both cantilever tips deflect under self-weight and prestress and keep moving with creep and shrinkage; when a drop-in is placed, its seat levels depend on the tip deflections of the two neighbouring main girders. If those girders differ in casting age, prestress or placement date, their creep rates differ and the drop-in ends end up at different levels.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：預製構件尺寸精準，放上去後的高程就不會再改變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Precast pieces are accurate, so their levels stay fixed after placement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主梁就位、掛梁與線形控制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Girder placement, drop-ins and alignment\" is correct?","options":["主梁放上墩頂後，兩側懸臂端會在自重與預力作用下產生撓度，並隨混凝土潛變與收縮持續變化；掛梁放入時，兩端支座的高程取決於相鄰兩支主梁的懸臂端撓度。","預製構件尺寸精準，放上去後的高程就不會再改變。","冰力很難量測，所以只能完全依賴設計規範的數值。"],"optionsEn":["Once a main girder is set on its pier, both cantilever tips deflect under self-weight and prestress and keep moving with creep and shrinkage.","Precast pieces are accurate, so their levels stay fixed after placement.","Ice forces cannot be measured, so engineers must rely entirely on code values."],"answer":0,"explanation":"主梁放上墩頂後，兩側懸臂端會在自重與預力作用下產生撓度，並隨混凝土潛變與收縮持續變化；掛梁放入時，兩端支座的高程取決於相鄰兩支主梁的懸臂端撓度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Once a main girder is set on its pier, both cantilever tips deflect under self-weight and prestress and keep moving with creep and shrinkage; when a drop-in is placed, its seat levels depend on the tip deflections of the two neighbouring main girders. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b014-v13-22","title":"主梁就位、掛梁與線形控制：定量估算","titleEn":"Girder placement, drop-ins and alignment: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「掛梁就位與懸臂端高差」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drop-in seating and tip level difference” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：懸臂端彈性撓度 40 mm，長期撓度 ≈ δ_el·(1+φ)。若甲主梁放置時齡期較長、φ = 1.5，長期撓度 40×2.5 = 100 mm；乙主梁較年輕、φ = 2.0，長期撓度 40×3.0 = 120 mm；兩端高差約 20 mm，需在掛梁座預留調整。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Elastic tip deflection is 40 mm and long-term deflection ≈ δ_el·(1+φ). An older girder with φ = 1.5 reaches 40×2.5 = 100 mm, while a younger one with φ = 2.0 reaches 40×3.0 = 120 mm; the 20 mm difference must be allowed for at the drop-in seats. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每支主梁從預製到放置定期量測懸臂端高程，以實測撓度修正潛變模型；掛梁就位前量測兩端座高差並依預測決定墊片厚度，完工後與一年後各量測一次全線縱斷面，確認長期變形符合預測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure tip levels of every main girder periodically from casting to placement and update the creep model with measured deflections; before seating a drop-in survey the seat level difference and choose shim thickness from predictions; survey the full profile at completion and again after a year to confirm long-term behaviour.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"懸臂端彈性撓度 40 mm，長期撓度 ≈ δ_el·(1+φ)。若甲主梁放置時齡期較長、φ = 1.5，長期撓度 40×2.5 = 100 mm；乙主梁較年輕、φ = 2.0，長期撓度 40×3.0 = 120 mm；兩端高差約 20 mm，需在掛梁座預留調整。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Elastic tip deflection is 40 mm and long-term deflection ≈ δ_el·(1+φ). An older girder with φ = 1.5 reaches 40×2.5 = 100 mm, while a younger one with φ = 2.0 reaches 40×3.0 = 120 mm; the 20 mm difference must be allowed for at the drop-in seats. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主梁就位、掛梁與線形控制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Girder placement, drop-ins and alignment\", which statement holds?","options":["鋪面只影響行車舒適，與結構壽命無關。","懸臂端彈性撓度 40 mm，長期撓度 ≈ δ_el·(1+φ)。","冰比混凝土軟得多，所以浮冰對橋墩的力量可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Surfacing only affects ride comfort and has nothing to do with structural life.","Elastic tip deflection is 40 mm and long-term deflection ≈ δ_el·(1+φ).","Ice is much softer than concrete, so pack-ice forces on piers are negligible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"懸臂端彈性撓度 40 mm，長期撓度 ≈ δ_el·(1+φ)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Elastic tip deflection is 40 mm and long-term deflection ≈ δ_el·(1+φ). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b014-v13-23","title":"主梁就位、掛梁與線形控制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Girder placement, drop-ins and alignment: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「掛梁就位與懸臂端高差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drop-in seating and tip level difference” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每支主梁從預製到放置定期量測懸臂端高程，以實測撓度修正潛變模型；掛梁就位前量測兩端座高差並依預測決定墊片厚度，完工後與一年後各量測一次全線縱斷面，確認長期變形符合預測。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure tip levels of every main girder periodically from casting to placement and update the creep model with measured deflections; before seating a drop-in survey the seat level difference and choose shim thickness from predictions; survey the full profile at completion and again after a year to confirm long-term behaviour. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：線形控制應有專責小組，建立每支主梁的齡期、預力與撓度紀錄，施工順序變更時重新預測並調整掛梁座；墊片或調整量的決定與實測值一併歸檔，交接後供維護單位判讀變形。","observationEn":"Site practice: A dedicated alignment team should keep age, prestress and deflection records for every main girder, re-predict and adjust seats whenever the sequence changes, and file each shim decision with its measurements for maintenance staff to interpret deformation after handover.","failure":"注意干擾：若只依設計理想齡期調整掛梁座，而實際施工順序改變，部分掛梁兩端高差逐年擴大，造成行車跳動、伸縮裝置受衝擊與防水層破壞；長期撓度大於預測時，橋面縱斷面出現連續起伏。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Setting drop-in seats for ideal design ages when the actual sequence changed lets level differences grow year by year, causing ride bumps, impact on expansion devices and torn waterproofing; long-term deflections larger than predicted leave a repeating wave in the profile. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每支主梁從預製到放置定期量測懸臂端高程，以實測撓度修正潛變模型；掛梁就位前量測兩端座高差並依預測決定墊片厚度，完工後與一年後各量測一次全線縱斷面，確認長期變形符合預測。","textEn":"Measure tip levels of every main girder periodically from casting to placement and update the creep model with measured deflections; before seating a drop-in survey the seat level difference and choose shim thickness from predictions; survey the full profile at completion and again after a year to confirm long-term behaviour.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"線形控制應有專責小組，建立每支主梁的齡期、預力與撓度紀錄，施工順序變更時重新預測並調整掛梁座；墊片或調整量的決定與實測值一併歸檔，交接後供維護單位判讀變形。","textEn":"A dedicated alignment team should keep age, prestress and deflection records for every main girder, re-predict and adjust seats whenever the sequence changes, and file each shim decision with its measurements for maintenance staff to interpret deformation after handover.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主梁就位、掛梁與線形控制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Girder placement, drop-ins and alignment\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","混凝土強度夠高，就能同時抵抗凍融、氯離子與冰磨蝕。","每支主梁從預製到放置定期量測懸臂端高程，以實測撓度修正潛變模型。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","High concrete strength alone resists freeze–thaw, chlorides and ice abrasion together.","Measure tip levels of every main girder periodically from casting to placement and update the creep model with measured deflections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每支主梁從預製到放置定期量測懸臂端高程，以實測撓度修正潛變模型；掛梁就位前量測兩端座高差並依預測決定墊片厚度，完工後與一年後各量測一次全線縱斷面，確認長期變形符合預測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure tip levels of every main girder periodically from casting to placement and update the creep model with measured deflections; before seating a drop-in survey the seat level difference and choose shim thickness from predictions; survey the full profile at completion and again after a year to confirm long-term behaviour. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b014-v13-24","title":"主梁就位、掛梁與線形控制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Girder placement, drop-ins and alignment: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「掛梁就位與懸臂端高差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drop-in seating and tip level difference” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只依設計理想齡期調整掛梁座，而實際施工順序改變，部分掛梁兩端高差逐年擴大，造成行車跳動、伸縮裝置受衝擊與防水層破壞；長期撓度大於預測時，橋面縱斷面出現連續起伏。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Setting drop-in seats for ideal design ages when the actual sequence changed lets level differences grow year by year, causing ride bumps, impact on expansion devices and torn waterproofing; long-term deflections larger than predicted leave a repeating wave in the profile. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：線形控制因此必須以時間為變數：預測每支主梁在放置掛梁時與長期的撓度，調整掛梁座高程或墊片，讓完工後的橋面縱斷面平順。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Alignment control must therefore treat time as a variable: predict each girder's deflection at drop-in placement and in the long term, and adjust seat levels or shims so the finished profile is smooth.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「預製構件尺寸精準，放上去後的高程就不會再改變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Precast pieces are accurate, so their levels stay fixed after placement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只依設計理想齡期調整掛梁座，而實際施工順序改變，部分掛梁兩端高差逐年擴大，造成行車跳動、伸縮裝置受衝擊與防水層破壞；長期撓度大於預測時，橋面縱斷面出現連續起伏。","textEn":"Setting drop-in seats for ideal design ages when the actual sequence changed lets level differences grow year by year, causing ride bumps, impact on expansion devices and torn waterproofing; long-term deflections larger than predicted leave a repeating wave in the profile.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主梁就位、掛梁與線形控制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Girder placement, drop-ins and alignment\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若只依設計理想齡期調整掛梁座，而實際施工順序改變，部分掛梁兩端高差逐年擴大，造成行車跳動、伸縮裝置受衝擊與防水層破壞。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","冰力很難量測，所以只能完全依賴設計規範的數值。"],"optionsEn":["Setting drop-in seats for ideal design ages when the actual sequence changed lets level differences grow year by year, causing ride bumps, impact on expansion devices and torn waterproofing.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Ice forces cannot be measured, so engineers must rely entirely on code values."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若只依設計理想齡期調整掛梁座，而實際施工順序改變，部分掛梁兩端高差逐年擴大，造成行車跳動、伸縮裝置受衝擊與防水層破壞；長期撓度大於預測時，橋面縱斷面出現連續起伏。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Setting drop-in seats for ideal design ages when the actual sequence changed lets level differences grow year by year, causing ride bumps, impact on expansion devices and torn waterproofing; long-term deflections larger than predicted leave a repeating wave in the profile. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b014-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「冰力與結構反應監測」與「強風管制與高側車輛」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Monitoring ice forces and response\" and \"Wind restrictions and high-sided vehicles\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b014-v13-25","title":"冰力與結構反應監測：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Monitoring ice forces and response: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「墩身傾斜計」如何影響聯邦大橋（加拿大）的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pier tiltmeters” governs force, deformation or durability in “Confederation Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"冰力的設計值帶有很大的不確定性：冰的強度隨溫度、鹽度與加載速率變化，冰板厚度與漂移速度年年不同。在代表性墩位裝設傾斜計、加速度計或應變計，再配合冰況觀測（冰厚、冰速、破壞模式），可以從結構反應反算實際冰力，檢驗設計假設，並為其他冰區橋梁累積資料。監測也能發現冰盾磨損或墩前堆冰改變受力模式的情況，作為冰季巡查與維修的依據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「墩身傾斜計」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Design ice forces carry large uncertainty: ice strength varies with temperature, salinity and loading rate, and sheet thickness and drift speed change from year to year. Tiltmeters, accelerometers or strain gauges on representative piers, combined with ice observations of thickness, speed and failure mode, let engineers back-calculate actual ice forces from structural response, test design assumptions and build data for other ice-exposed bridges. Monitoring also reveals when shield wear or rubble build-up changes the loading mode, guiding ice-season patrols and repairs. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Pier tiltmeters” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以墩身轉動勁度 k_θ = 5×10⁸ kN·m/rad 反算：量到冰作用時墩頂附加傾角 θ = 20 μrad，彎矩 M = k_θ·θ = 5×10⁸×20×10⁻⁶ = 10,000 kN·m；若作用點到轉動中心的力臂 30 m，冰力 F = 10,000/30 ≈ 333 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Back-calculate with a pier rotational stiffness k_θ = 5×10⁸ kN·m/rad: an extra tilt θ = 20 μrad during an ice event gives M = k_θ·θ = 5×10⁸×20×10⁻⁶ = 10,000 kN·m, and with a 30 m lever arm to the rotation centre the ice force is F = 10,000/30 ≈ 333 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「冰力很難量測，所以只能完全依賴設計規範的數值。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Ice forces cannot be measured, so engineers must rely entirely on code values.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「墩身傾斜計」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Pier tiltmeters”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-25-k1","title":"冰力與結構反應監測","titleEn":"Monitoring ice forces and response","text":"冰力的設計值帶有很大的不確定性：冰的強度隨溫度、鹽度與加載速率變化，冰板厚度與漂移速度年年不同。在代表性墩位裝設傾斜計、加速度計或應變計，再配合冰況觀測（冰厚、冰速、破壞模式），可以從結構反應反算實際冰力，檢驗設計假設，並為其他冰區橋梁累積資料。","textEn":"Design ice forces carry large uncertainty: ice strength varies with temperature, salinity and loading rate, and sheet thickness and drift speed change from year to year. Tiltmeters, accelerometers or strain gauges on representative piers, combined with ice observations of thickness, speed and failure mode, let engineers back-calculate actual ice forces from structural response, test design assumptions and build data for other ice-exposed bridges.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：冰力很難量測，所以只能完全依賴設計規範的數值。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Ice forces cannot be measured, so engineers must rely entirely on code values. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「冰力與結構反應監測」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Monitoring ice forces and response\" is correct?","options":["冰力很難量測，所以只能完全依賴設計規範的數值。","冰力的設計值帶有很大的不確定性：冰的強度隨溫度、鹽度與加載速率變化，冰板厚度與漂移速度年年不同。","只要橋梁結構能承受颱風等級的風，車輛在橋上就一定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Ice forces cannot be measured, so engineers must rely entirely on code values.","Design ice forces carry large uncertainty: ice strength varies with temperature, salinity and loading rate, and sheet thickness and drift speed change from year to year.","If the structure can withstand storm winds, vehicles on it are automatically safe."],"answer":1,"explanation":"冰力的設計值帶有很大的不確定性：冰的強度隨溫度、鹽度與加載速率變化，冰板厚度與漂移速度年年不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Design ice forces carry large uncertainty: ice strength varies with temperature, salinity and loading rate, and sheet thickness and drift speed change from year to year. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b014-v13-26","title":"冰力與結構反應監測：定量估算","titleEn":"Monitoring ice forces and response: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「墩身傾斜計」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pier tiltmeters” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以墩身轉動勁度 k_θ = 5×10⁸ kN·m/rad 反算：量到冰作用時墩頂附加傾角 θ = 20 μrad，彎矩 M = k_θ·θ = 5×10⁸×20×10⁻⁶ = 10,000 kN·m；若作用點到轉動中心的力臂 30 m，冰力 F = 10,000/30 ≈ 333 kN。勁度與力臂為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Back-calculate with a pier rotational stiffness k_θ = 5×10⁸ kN·m/rad: an extra tilt θ = 20 μrad during an ice event gives M = k_θ·θ = 5×10⁸×20×10⁻⁶ = 10,000 kN·m, and with a 30 m lever arm to the rotation centre the ice force is F = 10,000/30 ≈ 333 kN. Stiffness and lever arm are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先以已知荷載（例如載重車或拉索施力）標定墩身的轉動勁度，再於冰季連續記錄傾角、溫度與冰況影像；以溫度修正排除日照造成的傾斜，比較反算冰力的統計分布與設計冰力，並檢查最大事件發生時的冰厚與破壞模式。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: First calibrate the pier's rotational stiffness with a known load such as test trucks or a cable pull, then log tilt, temperature and ice imagery continuously through the ice season; remove sun-induced tilt by temperature correction, compare the statistical distribution of back-calculated forces with design ice loads, and check ice thickness and failure mode during the largest events.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以墩身轉動勁度 k_θ = 5×10⁸ kN·m/rad 反算：量到冰作用時墩頂附加傾角 θ = 20 μrad，彎矩 M = k_θ·θ = 5×10⁸×20×10⁻⁶ = 10,000 kN·m；若作用點到轉動中心的力臂 30 m，冰力 F = 10,000/30 ≈ 333 kN。勁度與力臂為教學假設。","textEn":"Back-calculate with a pier rotational stiffness k_θ = 5×10⁸ kN·m/rad: an extra tilt θ = 20 μrad during an ice event gives M = k_θ·θ = 5×10⁸×20×10⁻⁶ = 10,000 kN·m, and with a 30 m lever arm to the rotation centre the ice force is F = 10,000/30 ≈ 333 kN. Stiffness and lever arm are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「冰力與結構反應監測」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Monitoring ice forces and response\", which statement holds?","options":["特許期結束時橋還能通車，就代表結構狀態良好。","預製構件只要在陸上做好，放到墩上就完成了結構體系。","以墩身轉動勁度 k_θ = 5×10⁸ kN·m/rad 反算：量到冰作用時墩頂附加傾角 θ = 20 μrad，彎矩 M = k_θ·θ = 5×10⁸×20×10⁻⁶ = 10,000 kN·m。"],"optionsEn":["If the bridge is still open at the end of the concession, its condition must be good.","Once precast pieces are made on land and set on the piers, the structural system is complete.","Back-calculate with a pier rotational stiffness k_θ = 5×10⁸ kN·m/rad: an extra tilt θ = 20 μrad during an ice event gives M = k_θ·θ = 5×10⁸×20×10⁻⁶ = 10,000 kN·m, and with a 30 m lever arm to the rotation centre the ice force is F = 10,000/30 ≈ 333 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以墩身轉動勁度 k_θ = 5×10⁸ kN·m/rad 反算：量到冰作用時墩頂附加傾角 θ = 20 μrad，彎矩 M = k_θ·θ = 5×10⁸×20×10⁻⁶ = 10,000 kN·m；若作用點到轉動中心的力臂 30 m，冰力 F = 10,000/30 ≈ 333 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Back-calculate with a pier rotational stiffness k_θ = 5×10⁸ kN·m/rad: an extra tilt θ = 20 μrad during an ice event gives M = k_θ·θ = 5×10⁸×20×10⁻⁶ = 10,000 kN·m, and with a 30 m lever arm to the rotation centre the ice force is F = 10,000/30 ≈ 333 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b014-v13-27","title":"冰力與結構反應監測：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Monitoring ice forces and response: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「墩身傾斜計」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pier tiltmeters” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先以已知荷載（例如載重車或拉索施力）標定墩身的轉動勁度，再於冰季連續記錄傾角、溫度與冰況影像；以溫度修正排除日照造成的傾斜，比較反算冰力的統計分布與設計冰力，並檢查最大事件發生時的冰厚與破壞模式。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"First calibrate the pier's rotational stiffness with a known load such as test trucks or a cable pull, then log tilt, temperature and ice imagery continuously through the ice season; remove sun-induced tilt by temperature correction, compare the statistical distribution of back-calculated forces with design ice loads, and check ice thickness and failure mode during the largest events. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：監測計畫應明訂標定方法、溫度修正、資料品質檢查與冰況同步觀測的方式，並指定判讀人員與年度報告格式；異常冰力事件後須進行墩身與冰盾的特別檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: The monitoring plan should define calibration, temperature correction, data-quality checks and synchronised ice observation, name the analysts and the annual report format, and require special inspection of pier and shield after any abnormal ice-force event.","failure":"注意干擾：若未做溫度修正，日照造成的墩身傾斜會被誤判為冰力，得出偏高或偏低的結論；感測器在冰季失效而未及時更換，正好錯過最需要的資料。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without temperature correction, sun-induced tilt is mistaken for ice load and leads to wrong conclusions; sensors that fail during the ice season and are not replaced miss exactly the data that matter most. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先以已知荷載（例如載重車或拉索施力）標定墩身的轉動勁度，再於冰季連續記錄傾角、溫度與冰況影像；以溫度修正排除日照造成的傾斜，比較反算冰力的統計分布與設計冰力，並檢查最大事件發生時的冰厚與破壞模式。","textEn":"First calibrate the pier's rotational stiffness with a known load such as test trucks or a cable pull, then log tilt, temperature and ice imagery continuously through the ice season; remove sun-induced tilt by temperature correction, compare the statistical distribution of back-calculated forces with design ice loads, and check ice thickness and failure mode during the largest events.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"監測計畫應明訂標定方法、溫度修正、資料品質檢查與冰況同步觀測的方式，並指定判讀人員與年度報告格式；異常冰力事件後須進行墩身與冰盾的特別檢查。","textEn":"The monitoring plan should define calibration, temperature correction, data-quality checks and synchronised ice observation, name the analysts and the annual report format, and require special inspection of pier and shield after any abnormal ice-force event.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「冰力與結構反應監測」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Monitoring ice forces and response\"?","options":["先以已知荷載（例如載重車或拉索施力）標定墩身的轉動勁度，再於冰季連續記錄傾角、溫度與冰況影像。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","預製構件夠重，疊上去後不需要灌漿或預力就能穩定傳力。"],"optionsEn":["First calibrate the pier's rotational stiffness with a known load such as test trucks or a cable pull, then log tilt, temperature and ice imagery continuously through the ice season.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Precast pieces are heavy enough to transmit load reliably when stacked, without grout or prestress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先以已知荷載（例如載重車或拉索施力）標定墩身的轉動勁度，再於冰季連續記錄傾角、溫度與冰況影像；以溫度修正排除日照造成的傾斜，比較反算冰力的統計分布與設計冰力，並檢查最大事件發生時的冰厚與破壞模式。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"First calibrate the pier's rotational stiffness with a known load such as test trucks or a cable pull, then log tilt, temperature and ice imagery continuously through the ice season; remove sun-induced tilt by temperature correction, compare the statistical distribution of back-calculated forces with design ice loads, and check ice thickness and failure mode during the largest events. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b014-v13-28","title":"冰力與結構反應監測：失效診斷","titleEn":"Monitoring ice forces and response: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「墩身傾斜計」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pier tiltmeters” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若未做溫度修正，日照造成的墩身傾斜會被誤判為冰力，得出偏高或偏低的結論；感測器在冰季失效而未及時更換，正好錯過最需要的資料。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without temperature correction, sun-induced tilt is mistaken for ice load and leads to wrong conclusions; sensors that fail during the ice season and are not replaced miss exactly the data that matter most. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：監測也能發現冰盾磨損或墩前堆冰改變受力模式的情況，作為冰季巡查與維修的依據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Monitoring also reveals when shield wear or rubble build-up changes the loading mode, guiding ice-season patrols and repairs.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「冰力很難量測，所以只能完全依賴設計規範的數值。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Ice forces cannot be measured, so engineers must rely entirely on code values.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若未做溫度修正，日照造成的墩身傾斜會被誤判為冰力，得出偏高或偏低的結論；感測器在冰季失效而未及時更換，正好錯過最需要的資料。","textEn":"Without temperature correction, sun-induced tilt is mistaken for ice load and leads to wrong conclusions; sensors that fail during the ice season and are not replaced miss exactly the data that matter most.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「冰力與結構反應監測」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Monitoring ice forces and response\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若未做溫度修正，日照造成的墩身傾斜會被誤判為冰力，得出偏高或偏低的結論；感測器在冰季失效而未及時更換，正好錯過最需要的資料。","只要橋梁結構能承受颱風等級的風，車輛在橋上就一定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Without temperature correction, sun-induced tilt is mistaken for ice load and leads to wrong conclusions.","If the structure can withstand storm winds, vehicles on it are automatically safe."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若未做溫度修正，日照造成的墩身傾斜會被誤判為冰力，得出偏高或偏低的結論；感測器在冰季失效而未及時更換，正好錯過最需要的資料。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without temperature correction, sun-induced tilt is mistaken for ice load and leads to wrong conclusions; sensors that fail during the ice season and are not replaced miss exactly the data that matter most. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b014-v13-29","title":"強風管制與高側車輛：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Wind restrictions and high-sided vehicles: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「橋面風速計」如何影響聯邦大橋（加拿大）的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Deck anemometers” governs force, deformation or durability in “Confederation Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"橋面大部分高出海面約 40 公尺，航道段最高約 60 公尺，海峽上的強風對結構通常不是控制因素，卻直接威脅高側車輛、空車拖車與機車的行車安全。營運單位在橋上設置風速計，官方網站每 6 分鐘更新持續風速與陣風，超過門檻時實施分級限制，例如禁止特定車種或降低速限。這是一種以量測支撐營運決策的措施：門檻值由車輛傾覆與側滑的力學計算決定，並以實際事故與風速紀錄修正。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「橋面風速計」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Most of the deck is about 40 m above the sea and up to about 60 m at the navigation span; strong winds over the strait rarely govern the structure but directly threaten high-sided vehicles, empty trailers and motorcycles. The operator runs deck anemometers, and its website updates sustained winds and gusts every six minutes, triggering staged restrictions such as banning certain vehicle types or lowering speed limits when thresholds are exceeded. It is a measurement-based operating decision: thresholds come from the mechanics of vehicle overturning and sliding, refined with incident and wind records. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Deck anemometers” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：陣風 107 km/h = 29.7 m/s，q = ½ρV² = 0.5×1.225×29.7² ≈ 541 Pa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 107 km/h gust is 29.7 m/s, so q = ½ρV² = 0.5×1.225×29.7² ≈ 541 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要橋梁結構能承受颱風等級的風，車輛在橋上就一定安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the structure can withstand storm winds, vehicles on it are automatically safe.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「橋面風速計」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Deck anemometers”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-29-k1","title":"強風管制與高側車輛","titleEn":"Wind restrictions and high-sided vehicles","text":"橋面大部分高出海面約 40 公尺，航道段最高約 60 公尺，海峽上的強風對結構通常不是控制因素，卻直接威脅高側車輛、空車拖車與機車的行車安全。營運單位在橋上設置風速計，官方網站每 6 分鐘更新持續風速與陣風，超過門檻時實施分級限制，例如禁止特定車種或降低速限。","textEn":"Most of the deck is about 40 m above the sea and up to about 60 m at the navigation span; strong winds over the strait rarely govern the structure but directly threaten high-sided vehicles, empty trailers and motorcycles. The operator runs deck anemometers, and its website updates sustained winds and gusts every six minutes, triggering staged restrictions such as banning certain vehicle types or lowering speed limits when thresholds are exceeded.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要橋梁結構能承受颱風等級的風，車輛在橋上就一定安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the structure can withstand storm winds, vehicles on it are automatically safe. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「強風管制與高側車輛」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wind restrictions and high-sided vehicles\" is correct?","options":["只要橋梁結構能承受颱風等級的風，車輛在橋上就一定安全。","鋪面只影響行車舒適，與結構壽命無關。","橋面大部分高出海面約 40 公尺，航道段最高約 60 公尺，海峽上的強風對結構通常不是控制因素，卻直接威脅高側車輛、空車拖車與機車的行車安全。"],"optionsEn":["If the structure can withstand storm winds, vehicles on it are automatically safe.","Surfacing only affects ride comfort and has nothing to do with structural life.","Most of the deck is about 40 m above the sea and up to about 60 m at the navigation span."],"answer":2,"explanation":"橋面大部分高出海面約 40 公尺，航道段最高約 60 公尺，海峽上的強風對結構通常不是控制因素，卻直接威脅高側車輛、空車拖車與機車的行車安全。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Most of the deck is about 40 m above the sea and up to about 60 m at the navigation span; strong winds over the strait rarely govern the structure but directly threaten high-sided vehicles, empty trailers and motorcycles. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b014-v13-30","title":"強風管制與高側車輛：定量估算","titleEn":"Wind restrictions and high-sided vehicles: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橋面風速計」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Deck anemometers” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：陣風 107 km/h = 29.7 m/s，q = ½ρV² = 0.5×1.225×29.7² ≈ 541 Pa。空拖車側面積 39 m²、側力係數 1.2：F = 541×1.2×39 ≈ 25.3 kN，作用高度 2.0 m，傾覆彎矩約 50.6 kN·m。空車重 80 kN、輪距半寬 1.0 m，抗傾覆彎矩 80 kN·m，安全係數約 1.58；滿載 300 kN 時約 5.9。車輛參數為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 107 km/h gust is 29.7 m/s, so q = ½ρV² = 0.5×1.225×29.7² ≈ 541 Pa. An empty trailer with 39 m² side area and side-force coefficient 1.2 sees F = 541×1.2×39 ≈ 25.3 kN at 2.0 m height, an overturning moment of about 50.6 kN·m. Weighing 80 kN with a half-track of 1.0 m, it resists 80 kN·m, a factor of about 1.58; loaded to 300 kN the factor is about 5.9. Vehicle parameters are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：風速計的位置、高度與遮蔽需與設計風場一致，並定期校正；以多年風速紀錄統計超過各門檻的時數，評估交通中斷的頻率；事故或車輛偏移事件發生時，回查當時風速與限制狀態，檢討門檻是否適當。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Anemometer position, height and shelter must match the design wind field, with regular calibration; multi-year wind records give the hours above each threshold and thus closure frequency; after incidents or vehicle drift events, review the wind speed and restriction status at the time to judge whether thresholds are right.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"陣風 107 km/h = 29.7 m/s，q = ½ρV² = 0.5×1.225×29.7² ≈ 541 Pa。空拖車側面積 39 m²、側力係數 1.2：F = 541×1.2×39 ≈ 25.3 kN，作用高度 2.0 m，傾覆彎矩約 50.6 kN·m。空車重 80 kN、輪距半寬 1.0 m，抗傾覆彎矩 80 kN·m，安全係數約 1.58；滿載 300 kN 時約 5.9。車輛參數為教學假設。","textEn":"A 107 km/h gust is 29.7 m/s, so q = ½ρV² = 0.5×1.225×29.7² ≈ 541 Pa. An empty trailer with 39 m² side area and side-force coefficient 1.2 sees F = 541×1.2×39 ≈ 25.3 kN at 2.0 m height, an overturning moment of about 50.6 kN·m. Weighing 80 kN with a half-track of 1.0 m, it resists 80 kN·m, a factor of about 1.58; loaded to 300 kN the factor is about 5.9. Vehicle parameters are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「強風管制與高側車輛」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wind restrictions and high-sided vehicles\", which statement holds?","options":["陣風 107 km/h = 29.7 m/s，q = ½ρV² = 0.5×1.225×29.7² ≈ 541 Pa。","冰比混凝土軟得多，所以浮冰對橋墩的力量可以忽略。","混凝土強度夠高，就能同時抵抗凍融、氯離子與冰磨蝕。"],"optionsEn":["A 107 km/h gust is 29.7 m/s, so q = ½ρV² = 0.5×1.225×29.7² ≈ 541 Pa.","Ice is much softer than concrete, so pack-ice forces on piers are negligible.","High concrete strength alone resists freeze–thaw, chlorides and ice abrasion together."],"answer":0,"explanation":"陣風 107 km/h = 29.7 m/s，q = ½ρV² = 0.5×1.225×29.7² ≈ 541 Pa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 107 km/h gust is 29.7 m/s, so q = ½ρV² = 0.5×1.225×29.7² ≈ 541 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b014-v13-31","title":"強風管制與高側車輛：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wind restrictions and high-sided vehicles: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橋面風速計」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Deck anemometers” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"風速計的位置、高度與遮蔽需與設計風場一致，並定期校正；以多年風速紀錄統計超過各門檻的時數，評估交通中斷的頻率；事故或車輛偏移事件發生時，回查當時風速與限制狀態，檢討門檻是否適當。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Anemometer position, height and shelter must match the design wind field, with regular calibration; multi-year wind records give the hours above each threshold and thus closure frequency; after incidents or vehicle drift events, review the wind speed and restriction status at the time to judge whether thresholds are right. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：營運手冊應列出各車種的風速門檻、量測來源、發布與解除程序及通報管道，並每年以事故與風速資料檢討；更換護欄或在橋面加裝設施時，須確認不影響風速計的代表性。","observationEn":"Site practice: The operating manual should list wind thresholds by vehicle type, measurement sources, procedures for issuing and lifting restrictions and communication channels, reviewed annually with incident and wind data; replacing barriers or adding deck equipment must not compromise anemometer representativeness.","failure":"注意干擾：風速計被結構或護欄遮蔽、量測偏低時，限制發布太晚，空車或高側車輛可能在陣風中偏移撞擊護欄甚至傾覆；門檻過於保守則頻繁封閉，影響島上物流與民生。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An anemometer sheltered by the structure or barriers reads low and restrictions come too late, so empty or high-sided vehicles can drift into barriers or overturn in gusts; overly conservative thresholds close the bridge often and disrupt island logistics and daily life. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"風速計的位置、高度與遮蔽需與設計風場一致，並定期校正；以多年風速紀錄統計超過各門檻的時數，評估交通中斷的頻率；事故或車輛偏移事件發生時，回查當時風速與限制狀態，檢討門檻是否適當。","textEn":"Anemometer position, height and shelter must match the design wind field, with regular calibration; multi-year wind records give the hours above each threshold and thus closure frequency; after incidents or vehicle drift events, review the wind speed and restriction status at the time to judge whether thresholds are right.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"營運手冊應列出各車種的風速門檻、量測來源、發布與解除程序及通報管道，並每年以事故與風速資料檢討；更換護欄或在橋面加裝設施時，須確認不影響風速計的代表性。","textEn":"The operating manual should list wind thresholds by vehicle type, measurement sources, procedures for issuing and lifting restrictions and communication channels, reviewed annually with incident and wind data; replacing barriers or adding deck equipment must not compromise anemometer representativeness.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「強風管制與高側車輛」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wind restrictions and high-sided vehicles\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","風速計的位置、高度與遮蔽需與設計風場一致，並定期校正。","只要浮吊能力夠大，工程進度就只取決於吊裝速度。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Anemometer position, height and shelter must match the design wind field, with regular calibration.","With a big enough crane, progress depends only on lifting speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"風速計的位置、高度與遮蔽需與設計風場一致，並定期校正；以多年風速紀錄統計超過各門檻的時數，評估交通中斷的頻率；事故或車輛偏移事件發生時，回查當時風速與限制狀態，檢討門檻是否適當。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Anemometer position, height and shelter must match the design wind field, with regular calibration; multi-year wind records give the hours above each threshold and thus closure frequency; after incidents or vehicle drift events, review the wind speed and restriction status at the time to judge whether thresholds are right. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b014-v13-32","title":"強風管制與高側車輛：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wind restrictions and high-sided vehicles: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橋面風速計」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Deck anemometers” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"風速計被結構或護欄遮蔽、量測偏低時，限制發布太晚，空車或高側車輛可能在陣風中偏移撞擊護欄甚至傾覆；門檻過於保守則頻繁封閉，影響島上物流與民生。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An anemometer sheltered by the structure or barriers reads low and restrictions come too late, so empty or high-sided vehicles can drift into barriers or overturn in gusts; overly conservative thresholds close the bridge often and disrupt island logistics and daily life. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這是一種以量測支撐營運決策的措施：門檻值由車輛傾覆與側滑的力學計算決定，並以實際事故與風速紀錄修正。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is a measurement-based operating decision: thresholds come from the mechanics of vehicle overturning and sliding, refined with incident and wind records.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要橋梁結構能承受颱風等級的風，車輛在橋上就一定安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the structure can withstand storm winds, vehicles on it are automatically safe.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"風速計被結構或護欄遮蔽、量測偏低時，限制發布太晚，空車或高側車輛可能在陣風中偏移撞擊護欄甚至傾覆；門檻過於保守則頻繁封閉，影響島上物流與民生。","textEn":"An anemometer sheltered by the structure or barriers reads low and restrictions come too late, so empty or high-sided vehicles can drift into barriers or overturn in gusts; overly conservative thresholds close the bridge often and disrupt island logistics and daily life.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「強風管制與高側車輛」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wind restrictions and high-sided vehicles\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鋪面只影響行車舒適，與結構壽命無關。","風速計被結構或護欄遮蔽、量測偏低時，限制發布太晚，空車或高側車輛可能在陣風中偏移撞擊護欄甚至傾覆；門檻過於保守則頻繁封閉，影響島上物流與民生。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Surfacing only affects ride comfort and has nothing to do with structural life.","An anemometer sheltered by the structure or barriers reads low and restrictions come too late, so empty or high-sided vehicles can drift into barriers or overturn in gusts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"風速計被結構或護欄遮蔽、量測偏低時，限制發布太晚，空車或高側車輛可能在陣風中偏移撞擊護欄甚至傾覆；門檻過於保守則頻繁封閉，影響島上物流與民生。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An anemometer sheltered by the structure or barriers reads low and restrictions come too late, so empty or high-sided vehicles can drift into barriers or overturn in gusts; overly conservative thresholds close the bridge often and disrupt island logistics and daily life. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b014-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「除冰鹽、凍融與橋面翻修」與「特許營運、年度檢查與 2032 交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"De-icing salt, freeze–thaw and resurfacing\" and \"Concession, inspections and the 2032 transfer\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b014-v13-33","title":"除冰鹽、凍融與橋面翻修：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"De-icing salt, freeze–thaw and resurfacing: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「橋面防水與鋪面」如何影響聯邦大橋（加拿大）的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Deck waterproofing and surfacing” governs force, deformation or durability in “Confederation Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"冬季除冰鹽讓橋面混凝土承受高濃度氯離子，加上反覆凍融，是橋面板最主要的劣化來源。橋面防水層與瀝青鋪面的任務就是把水和鹽擋在結構混凝土之外；營運單位說明 2015 年做過微表處理，近期又進行自通車以來最大規模的鋪面更新，目的之一正是防止水與除冰鹽進入結構橋面板，以確保 100 年壽命。鋪面是犧牲層，必須定期更換；施工時刨除舊鋪面若傷及防水層或橋面板，反而會縮短結構壽命。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「橋面防水與鋪面」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Winter de-icing salt loads the deck concrete with high chloride concentrations, which together with repeated freeze–thaw is the main deterioration source for the deck slab. The waterproofing membrane and asphalt surfacing exist to keep water and salt out of the structural concrete; the operator explains that micro-surfacing was done in 2015 and that a recent resurfacing, the largest since opening, aimed partly at keeping water and de-icing salt out of the structural deck to secure the 100-year life. Surfacing is a sacrificial layer that must be renewed periodically, and milling that damages the membrane or the slab shortens the structure's life instead. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Deck waterproofing and surfacing” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：ASTM C666 耐久因數 DF = P·N/M：300 次凍融循環後相對動彈性模數 P = 90%，DF = 90×300/300 = 90。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: ASTM C666 durability factor DF = P·N/M: with relative dynamic modulus P = 90% after 300 cycles, DF = 90×300/300 = 90.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋪面只影響行車舒適，與結構壽命無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Surfacing only affects ride comfort and has nothing to do with structural life.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「橋面防水與鋪面」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Deck waterproofing and surfacing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-33-k1","title":"除冰鹽、凍融與橋面翻修","titleEn":"De-icing salt, freeze–thaw and resurfacing","text":"冬季除冰鹽讓橋面混凝土承受高濃度氯離子，加上反覆凍融，是橋面板最主要的劣化來源。橋面防水層與瀝青鋪面的任務就是把水和鹽擋在結構混凝土之外；營運單位說明 2015 年做過微表處理，近期又進行自通車以來最大規模的鋪面更新，目的之一正是防止水與除冰鹽進入結構橋面板，以確保 100 年壽命。","textEn":"Winter de-icing salt loads the deck concrete with high chloride concentrations, which together with repeated freeze–thaw is the main deterioration source for the deck slab. The waterproofing membrane and asphalt surfacing exist to keep water and salt out of the structural concrete; the operator explains that micro-surfacing was done in 2015 and that a recent resurfacing, the largest since opening, aimed partly at keeping water and de-icing salt out of the structural deck to secure the 100-year life.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋪面只影響行車舒適，與結構壽命無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Surfacing only affects ride comfort and has nothing to do with structural life. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「除冰鹽、凍融與橋面翻修」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"De-icing salt, freeze–thaw and resurfacing\" is correct?","options":["冬季除冰鹽讓橋面混凝土承受高濃度氯離子，加上反覆凍融，是橋面板最主要的劣化來源。","鋪面只影響行車舒適，與結構壽命無關。","特許期結束時橋還能通車，就代表結構狀態良好。"],"optionsEn":["Winter de-icing salt loads the deck concrete with high chloride concentrations, which together with repeated freeze–thaw is the main deterioration source for the deck slab.","Surfacing only affects ride comfort and has nothing to do with structural life.","If the bridge is still open at the end of the concession, its condition must be good."],"answer":0,"explanation":"冬季除冰鹽讓橋面混凝土承受高濃度氯離子，加上反覆凍融，是橋面板最主要的劣化來源。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Winter de-icing salt loads the deck concrete with high chloride concentrations, which together with repeated freeze–thaw is the main deterioration source for the deck slab. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b014-v13-34","title":"除冰鹽、凍融與橋面翻修：定量估算","titleEn":"De-icing salt, freeze–thaw and resurfacing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橋面防水與鋪面」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Deck waterproofing and surfacing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：ASTM C666 耐久因數 DF = P·N/M：300 次凍融循環後相對動彈性模數 P = 90%，DF = 90×300/300 = 90。若每年約 60 次凍融、100 年約 6,000 次，遠多於試驗的 300 次，所以試驗結果只能作為配比比較，必須配合防水層把橋面混凝土保持在低含水狀態。凍融次數為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: ASTM C666 durability factor DF = P·N/M: with relative dynamic modulus P = 90% after 300 cycles, DF = 90×300/300 = 90. At about 60 freeze–thaw cycles a year, 100 years bring about 6,000 cycles, far beyond the 300 tested, so the test only ranks mixes and the membrane must keep the deck concrete dry. The cycle count is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：鋪面翻修前以透地雷達或鑽心檢查防水層與橋面板狀況，刨除時控制刨深並檢查有無傷及防水層；新鋪面驗收壓實度、厚度與平整度；定期在代表性位置量測橋面板氯離子含量與半電池電位，追蹤腐蝕風險。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before resurfacing check the membrane and slab by ground-penetrating radar or cores, control milling depth and look for membrane damage; accept the new surfacing on compaction, thickness and smoothness; periodically measure chloride content and half-cell potential at representative deck locations to track corrosion risk.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"ASTM C666 耐久因數 DF = P·N/M：300 次凍融循環後相對動彈性模數 P = 90%，DF = 90×300/300 = 90。若每年約 60 次凍融、100 年約 6,000 次，遠多於試驗的 300 次，所以試驗結果只能作為配比比較，必須配合防水層把橋面混凝土保持在低含水狀態。凍融次數為教學假設。","textEn":"ASTM C666 durability factor DF = P·N/M: with relative dynamic modulus P = 90% after 300 cycles, DF = 90×300/300 = 90. At about 60 freeze–thaw cycles a year, 100 years bring about 6,000 cycles, far beyond the 300 tested, so the test only ranks mixes and the membrane must keep the deck concrete dry. The cycle count is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「除冰鹽、凍融與橋面翻修」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"De-icing salt, freeze–thaw and resurfacing\", which statement holds?","options":["預製構件只要在陸上做好，放到墩上就完成了結構體系。","ASTM C666 耐久因數 DF = P·N/M：300 次凍融循環後相對動彈性模數 P = 90%，DF = 90×300/300 = 90。","預製構件夠重，疊上去後不需要灌漿或預力就能穩定傳力。"],"optionsEn":["Once precast pieces are made on land and set on the piers, the structural system is complete.","ASTM C666 durability factor DF = P·N/M: with relative dynamic modulus P = 90% after 300 cycles, DF = 90×300/300 = 90.","Precast pieces are heavy enough to transmit load reliably when stacked, without grout or prestress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"ASTM C666 耐久因數 DF = P·N/M：300 次凍融循環後相對動彈性模數 P = 90%，DF = 90×300/300 = 90。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"ASTM C666 durability factor DF = P·N/M: with relative dynamic modulus P = 90% after 300 cycles, DF = 90×300/300 = 90. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b014-v13-35","title":"除冰鹽、凍融與橋面翻修：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"De-icing salt, freeze–thaw and resurfacing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橋面防水與鋪面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Deck waterproofing and surfacing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"鋪面翻修前以透地雷達或鑽心檢查防水層與橋面板狀況，刨除時控制刨深並檢查有無傷及防水層；新鋪面驗收壓實度、厚度與平整度；定期在代表性位置量測橋面板氯離子含量與半電池電位，追蹤腐蝕風險。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before resurfacing check the membrane and slab by ground-penetrating radar or cores, control milling depth and look for membrane damage; accept the new surfacing on compaction, thickness and smoothness; periodically measure chloride content and half-cell potential at representative deck locations to track corrosion risk. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：鋪面翻修規範應包含刨深控制、防水層檢查與修補、交通維持與冬季前完工的期限；每次翻修後更新橋面板狀況紀錄，並在交接文件中記錄防水層系統與歷次翻修資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Resurfacing specifications should cover milling-depth control, membrane inspection and repair, traffic management and a completion deadline before winter; update the deck condition record after each campaign and include the membrane system and resurfacing history in handover documents.","failure":"注意干擾：鋪面裂縫與坑洞若長期不修，鹽水直接滲入橋面板，鋼筋腐蝕膨脹使橋面板底部剝落；刨除過深傷到防水層後重鋪，表面看似全新，內部卻失去防水保護。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Long-unrepaired cracks and potholes let brine soak into the slab, and corroding bars spall its soffit; milling too deep and damaging the membrane before repaving leaves a surface that looks new while the deck has lost its waterproofing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"鋪面翻修前以透地雷達或鑽心檢查防水層與橋面板狀況，刨除時控制刨深並檢查有無傷及防水層；新鋪面驗收壓實度、厚度與平整度；定期在代表性位置量測橋面板氯離子含量與半電池電位，追蹤腐蝕風險。","textEn":"Before resurfacing check the membrane and slab by ground-penetrating radar or cores, control milling depth and look for membrane damage; accept the new surfacing on compaction, thickness and smoothness; periodically measure chloride content and half-cell potential at representative deck locations to track corrosion risk.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"鋪面翻修規範應包含刨深控制、防水層檢查與修補、交通維持與冬季前完工的期限；每次翻修後更新橋面板狀況紀錄，並在交接文件中記錄防水層系統與歷次翻修資料。","textEn":"Resurfacing specifications should cover milling-depth control, membrane inspection and repair, traffic management and a completion deadline before winter; update the deck condition record after each campaign and include the membrane system and resurfacing history in handover documents.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「除冰鹽、凍融與橋面翻修」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"De-icing salt, freeze–thaw and resurfacing\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","預製構件尺寸精準，放上去後的高程就不會再改變。","鋪面翻修前以透地雷達或鑽心檢查防水層與橋面板狀況，刨除時控制刨深並檢查有無傷及防水層。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Precast pieces are accurate, so their levels stay fixed after placement.","Before resurfacing check the membrane and slab by ground-penetrating radar or cores, control milling depth and look for membrane damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鋪面翻修前以透地雷達或鑽心檢查防水層與橋面板狀況，刨除時控制刨深並檢查有無傷及防水層；新鋪面驗收壓實度、厚度與平整度；定期在代表性位置量測橋面板氯離子含量與半電池電位，追蹤腐蝕風險。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before resurfacing check the membrane and slab by ground-penetrating radar or cores, control milling depth and look for membrane damage; accept the new surfacing on compaction, thickness and smoothness; periodically measure chloride content and half-cell potential at representative deck locations to track corrosion risk. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b014-v13-36","title":"除冰鹽、凍融與橋面翻修：失效診斷","titleEn":"De-icing salt, freeze–thaw and resurfacing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橋面防水與鋪面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Deck waterproofing and surfacing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"鋪面裂縫與坑洞若長期不修，鹽水直接滲入橋面板，鋼筋腐蝕膨脹使橋面板底部剝落；刨除過深傷到防水層後重鋪，表面看似全新，內部卻失去防水保護。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Long-unrepaired cracks and potholes let brine soak into the slab, and corroding bars spall its soffit; milling too deep and damaging the membrane before repaving leaves a surface that looks new while the deck has lost its waterproofing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：鋪面是犧牲層，必須定期更換；施工時刨除舊鋪面若傷及防水層或橋面板，反而會縮短結構壽命。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Surfacing is a sacrificial layer that must be renewed periodically, and milling that damages the membrane or the slab shortens the structure's life instead.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋪面只影響行車舒適，與結構壽命無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Surfacing only affects ride comfort and has nothing to do with structural life.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鋪面裂縫與坑洞若長期不修，鹽水直接滲入橋面板，鋼筋腐蝕膨脹使橋面板底部剝落；刨除過深傷到防水層後重鋪，表面看似全新，內部卻失去防水保護。","textEn":"Long-unrepaired cracks and potholes let brine soak into the slab, and corroding bars spall its soffit; milling too deep and damaging the membrane before repaving leaves a surface that looks new while the deck has lost its waterproofing.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「除冰鹽、凍融與橋面翻修」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"De-icing salt, freeze–thaw and resurfacing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["鋪面裂縫與坑洞若長期不修，鹽水直接滲入橋面板，鋼筋腐蝕膨脹使橋面板底部剝落；刨除過深傷到防水層後重鋪，表面看似全新，內部卻失去防水保護。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","特許期結束時橋還能通車，就代表結構狀態良好。"],"optionsEn":["Long-unrepaired cracks and potholes let brine soak into the slab, and corroding bars spall its soffit.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If the bridge is still open at the end of the concession, its condition must be good."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鋪面裂縫與坑洞若長期不修，鹽水直接滲入橋面板，鋼筋腐蝕膨脹使橋面板底部剝落；刨除過深傷到防水層後重鋪，表面看似全新，內部卻失去防水保護。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Long-unrepaired cracks and potholes let brine soak into the slab, and corroding bars spall its soffit; milling too deep and damaging the membrane before repaving leaves a surface that looks new while the deck has lost its waterproofing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b014-v13-37","title":"特許營運、年度檢查與 2032 交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Concession, inspections and the 2032 transfer: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「2032 年交接文件」如何影響聯邦大橋（加拿大）的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “2032 transfer records” governs force, deformation or durability in “Confederation Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"聯邦大橋屬於加拿大聯邦資產，由 Strait Crossing 公司依 1993 年協議設計、興建、融資、營運與維護，營運期至 2032 年，之後移交加拿大政府；公共服務及採購部表示仍進行年度檢查與預防性維護。這種長期特許模式把維護責任與收費收入綁在一起，但移交時點的狀態定義至關重要：新管理者需要知道結構已用掉多少壽命、哪些構件接近劣化門檻、哪些監測資料可用。交接文件因此要回答「現況是否符合百年設計壽命的軌跡」。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「2032 年交接文件」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Confederation Bridge is a federal asset designed, built, financed, operated and maintained by Strait Crossing under 1993 agreements, operating until 2032 when it passes to the Government of Canada; Public Services and Procurement Canada states that it continues annual inspections and preventive maintenance. Such a long concession ties maintenance to toll revenue, but defining condition at the transfer date is critical: the new manager must know how much life has been used, which components are near deterioration thresholds and what monitoring data exist. Handover documents must therefore answer whether the bridge is on track for its 100-year life. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “2032 transfer records” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：1997 年通車到 2032 年移交共 35 年，佔 100 年設計壽命的 35/100 = 35%，剩餘約 65 年（2016 年預算官報告估計壽命至 2097 年）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: From opening in 1997 to transfer in 2032 is 35 years, 35/100 = 35% of the design life, leaving about 65 years (a 2016 budget-officer report put the end of life at 2097).","failure":"常見誤解：「特許期結束時橋還能通車，就代表結構狀態良好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the bridge is still open at the end of the concession, its condition must be good.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「2032 年交接文件」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “2032 transfer records”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-37-k1","title":"特許營運、年度檢查與 2032 交接","titleEn":"Concession, inspections and the 2032 transfer","text":"聯邦大橋屬於加拿大聯邦資產，由 Strait Crossing 公司依 1993 年協議設計、興建、融資、營運與維護，營運期至 2032 年，之後移交加拿大政府；公共服務及採購部表示仍進行年度檢查與預防性維護。這種長期特許模式把維護責任與收費收入綁在一起，但移交時點的狀態定義至關重要：新管理者需要知道結構已用掉多少壽命、哪些構件接近劣化門檻、哪些監測資料可用。","textEn":"Confederation Bridge is a federal asset designed, built, financed, operated and maintained by Strait Crossing under 1993 agreements, operating until 2032 when it passes to the Government of Canada; Public Services and Procurement Canada states that it continues annual inspections and preventive maintenance. Such a long concession ties maintenance to toll revenue, but defining condition at the transfer date is critical: the new manager must know how much life has been used, which components are near deterioration thresholds and what monitoring data exist.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：特許期結束時橋還能通車，就代表結構狀態良好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the bridge is still open at the end of the concession, its condition must be good. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「特許營運、年度檢查與 2032 交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Concession, inspections and the 2032 transfer\" is correct?","options":["特許期結束時橋還能通車，就代表結構狀態良好。","聯邦大橋屬於加拿大聯邦資產，由 Strait Crossing 公司依 1993 年協議設計、興建、融資、營運與維護，營運期至 2032 年，之後移交加拿大政府。","冰比混凝土軟得多，所以浮冰對橋墩的力量可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["If the bridge is still open at the end of the concession, its condition must be good.","Confederation Bridge is a federal asset designed, built, financed, operated and maintained by Strait Crossing under 1993 agreements, operating until 2032 when it passes to the Government of Canada.","Ice is much softer than concrete, so pack-ice forces on piers are negligible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"聯邦大橋屬於加拿大聯邦資產，由 Strait Crossing 公司依 1993 年協議設計、興建、融資、營運與維護，營運期至 2032 年，之後移交加拿大政府；公共服務及採購部表示仍進行年度檢查與預防性維護。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Confederation Bridge is a federal asset designed, built, financed, operated and maintained by Strait Crossing under 1993 agreements, operating until 2032 when it passes to the Government of Canada; Public Services and Procurement Canada states that it continues annual inspections and preventive maintenance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b014-v13-38","title":"特許營運、年度檢查與 2032 交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Concession, inspections and the 2032 transfer: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「2032 年交接文件」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “2032 transfer records” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：1997 年通車到 2032 年移交共 35 年，佔 100 年設計壽命的 35/100 = 35%，剩餘約 65 年（2016 年預算官報告估計壽命至 2097 年）。若某暴露區預測在第 60 年開始腐蝕，即約 2057 年，移交後只有 25 年可規劃修繕。腐蝕起始年份為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: From opening in 1997 to transfer in 2032 is 35 years, 35/100 = 35% of the design life, leaving about 65 years (a 2016 budget-officer report put the end of life at 2097). If one exposure zone is predicted to start corroding at year 60, about 2057, only 25 years remain after transfer to plan repairs. The initiation year is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：移交前由雙方共同委託獨立檢查，依構件逐項評定狀況等級，並以氯離子剖面、保護層、預力孔道與冰盾磨蝕的量測資料推估剩餘壽命；比較歷年年度檢查紀錄的趨勢，確認劣化速率與百年設計的假設一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before transfer both parties commission an independent inspection that rates every component, and estimate remaining life from chloride profiles, cover, tendon-duct and ice-shield abrasion data; compare trends in years of annual inspection records to confirm deterioration rates consistent with the 100-year assumptions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"1997 年通車到 2032 年移交共 35 年，佔 100 年設計壽命的 35/100 = 35%，剩餘約 65 年（2016 年預算官報告估計壽命至 2097 年）。若某暴露區預測在第 60 年開始腐蝕，即約 2057 年，移交後只有 25 年可規劃修繕。腐蝕起始年份為教學假設。","textEn":"From opening in 1997 to transfer in 2032 is 35 years, 35/100 = 35% of the design life, leaving about 65 years (a 2016 budget-officer report put the end of life at 2097). If one exposure zone is predicted to start corroding at year 60, about 2057, only 25 years remain after transfer to plan repairs. The initiation year is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「特許營運、年度檢查與 2032 交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Concession, inspections and the 2032 transfer\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土強度夠高，就能同時抵抗凍融、氯離子與冰磨蝕。","只要浮吊能力夠大，工程進度就只取決於吊裝速度。","1997 年通車到 2032 年移交共 35 年，佔 100 年設計壽命的 35/100 = 35%，剩餘約 65 年（2016 年預算官報告估計壽命至 2097 年）。"],"optionsEn":["High concrete strength alone resists freeze–thaw, chlorides and ice abrasion together.","With a big enough crane, progress depends only on lifting speed.","From opening in 1997 to transfer in 2032 is 35 years, 35/100 = 35% of the design life, leaving about 65 years (a 2016 budget-officer report put the end of life at 2097)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"1997 年通車到 2032 年移交共 35 年，佔 100 年設計壽命的 35/100 = 35%，剩餘約 65 年（2016 年預算官報告估計壽命至 2097 年）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"From opening in 1997 to transfer in 2032 is 35 years, 35/100 = 35% of the design life, leaving about 65 years (a 2016 budget-officer report put the end of life at 2097). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b014-v13-39","title":"特許營運、年度檢查與 2032 交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Concession, inspections and the 2032 transfer: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「2032 年交接文件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “2032 transfer records” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"移交前由雙方共同委託獨立檢查，依構件逐項評定狀況等級，並以氯離子剖面、保護層、預力孔道與冰盾磨蝕的量測資料推估剩餘壽命；比較歷年年度檢查紀錄的趨勢，確認劣化速率與百年設計的假設一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before transfer both parties commission an independent inspection that rates every component, and estimate remaining life from chloride profiles, cover, tendon-duct and ice-shield abrasion data; compare trends in years of annual inspection records to confirm deterioration rates consistent with the 100-year assumptions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：特許合約應事先訂定移交時的狀態標準、必須提交的檢查與量測資料、剩餘壽命評估方法與缺失處理方式；移交文件包含竣工圖、構件履歷、年度檢查、監測資料與維修紀錄，並由獨立工程師簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The concession agreement should define in advance the condition standard at transfer, required inspection and measurement data, the remaining-life method and how defects are handled; transfer documents include as-built drawings, component histories, annual inspections, monitoring data and repair records, signed off by an independent engineer.","failure":"注意干擾：若移交只看外觀而未量測隱蔽劣化，新管理者可能在接手數年後才發現預力孔道或橋面板的嚴重問題，修繕責任與費用產生爭議；監測資料格式不明或基準遺失，則多年資料無法比較。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A transfer based on appearance without measuring hidden deterioration may leave the new manager discovering serious tendon or deck problems a few years later, with disputes over responsibility and cost; unclear data formats or lost baselines make years of monitoring incomparable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"移交前由雙方共同委託獨立檢查，依構件逐項評定狀況等級，並以氯離子剖面、保護層、預力孔道與冰盾磨蝕的量測資料推估剩餘壽命；比較歷年年度檢查紀錄的趨勢，確認劣化速率與百年設計的假設一致。","textEn":"Before transfer both parties commission an independent inspection that rates every component, and estimate remaining life from chloride profiles, cover, tendon-duct and ice-shield abrasion data; compare trends in years of annual inspection records to confirm deterioration rates consistent with the 100-year assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"特許合約應事先訂定移交時的狀態標準、必須提交的檢查與量測資料、剩餘壽命評估方法與缺失處理方式；移交文件包含竣工圖、構件履歷、年度檢查、監測資料與維修紀錄，並由獨立工程師簽認。","textEn":"The concession agreement should define in advance the condition standard at transfer, required inspection and measurement data, the remaining-life method and how defects are handled; transfer documents include as-built drawings, component histories, annual inspections, monitoring data and repair records, signed off by an independent engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「特許營運、年度檢查與 2032 交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Concession, inspections and the 2032 transfer\"?","options":["移交前由雙方共同委託獨立檢查，依構件逐項評定狀況等級，並以氯離子剖面、保護層、預力孔道與冰盾磨蝕的量測資料推估剩餘壽命。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","冰力很難量測，所以只能完全依賴設計規範的數值。"],"optionsEn":["Before transfer both parties commission an independent inspection that rates every component, and estimate remaining life from chloride profiles, cover, tendon-duct and ice-shield abrasion data.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Ice forces cannot be measured, so engineers must rely entirely on code values."],"answer":0,"explanation":"移交前由雙方共同委託獨立檢查，依構件逐項評定狀況等級，並以氯離子剖面、保護層、預力孔道與冰盾磨蝕的量測資料推估剩餘壽命；比較歷年年度檢查紀錄的趨勢，確認劣化速率與百年設計的假設一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before transfer both parties commission an independent inspection that rates every component, and estimate remaining life from chloride profiles, cover, tendon-duct and ice-shield abrasion data; compare trends in years of annual inspection records to confirm deterioration rates consistent with the 100-year assumptions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b014-v13-40","title":"特許營運、年度檢查與 2032 交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Concession, inspections and the 2032 transfer: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b014-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「2032 年交接文件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “2032 transfer records” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若移交只看外觀而未量測隱蔽劣化，新管理者可能在接手數年後才發現預力孔道或橋面板的嚴重問題，修繕責任與費用產生爭議；監測資料格式不明或基準遺失，則多年資料無法比較。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A transfer based on appearance without measuring hidden deterioration may leave the new manager discovering serious tendon or deck problems a few years later, with disputes over responsibility and cost; unclear data formats or lost baselines make years of monitoring incomparable. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：交接文件因此要回答「現況是否符合百年設計壽命的軌跡」。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Handover documents must therefore answer whether the bridge is on track for its 100-year life.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「特許期結束時橋還能通車，就代表結構狀態良好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the bridge is still open at the end of the concession, its condition must be good.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b014-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若移交只看外觀而未量測隱蔽劣化，新管理者可能在接手數年後才發現預力孔道或橋面板的嚴重問題，修繕責任與費用產生爭議；監測資料格式不明或基準遺失，則多年資料無法比較。","textEn":"A transfer based on appearance without measuring hidden deterioration may leave the new manager discovering serious tendon or deck problems a few years later, with disputes over responsibility and cost; unclear data formats or lost baselines make years of monitoring incomparable.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]},{"id":"b014-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「特許營運、年度檢查與 2032 交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Concession, inspections and the 2032 transfer\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若移交只看外觀而未量測隱蔽劣化，新管理者可能在接手數年後才發現預力孔道或橋面板的嚴重問題，修繕責任與費用產生爭議。","冰比混凝土軟得多，所以浮冰對橋墩的力量可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A transfer based on appearance without measuring hidden deterioration may leave the new manager discovering serious tendon or deck problems a few years later, with disputes over responsibility and cost.","Ice is much softer than concrete, so pack-ice forces on piers are negligible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若移交只看外觀而未量測隱蔽劣化，新管理者可能在接手數年後才發現預力孔道或橋面板的嚴重問題，修繕責任與費用產生爭議；監測資料格式不明或基準遺失，則多年資料無法比較。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A transfer based on appearance without measuring hidden deterioration may leave the new manager discovering serious tendon or deck problems a few years later, with disputes over responsibility and cost; unclear data formats or lost baselines make years of monitoring incomparable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-scbl-about-us","v13s-pspc-confederation-bridge","v13s-tc-confederation-briefing","v13s-canadian-encyclopedia-bridge","v13s-wiki-confederation-bridge"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
